{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":307,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T00:11:14.947060276Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"55c73bbe-48d1-4e77-810f-0247f3ad4bda","comment_uuid":"84d67b48-5363-4613-9735-f069054e9ab4","author":"OL2r","content":"CORRECTION — AC-3 retried with opencode/big-pickle as auditor. COMPLETED in ~8 min with CONDITIONAL PASS (vs North Mini's 31-min loop / no completion). Big Pickle identified the true root cause of the earlier AC-3 failures: a HARNESS PERMISSION-ENFORCEMENT DEFECT, not a model-capability issue. The read-only sandbox deterministically denies git status/log/diff, ls, cat, echo, pwd despite .opencode/agents/*.md, hook-config allowed_bash_prefixes, and KICKOFF.md all declaring them allowed (only 'crosslink *' executes). North Mini hit the identical denials. My earlier '#78 misattribution' entry (AC-3 = model-capability finding, NOT pipeline defect) is WRONG and should be amended: the sandbox drift is a pipeline defect; model discipline is secondary.\n\nBig Pickle full audit (observation #75 on #108): AC-1/AC-2/AC-4 PASS stand; AC-3 now CONDITIONAL PASS. Other findings: (1) cross-worktree artifact handoff not exercised, (2) no dependency encoding, (3) findings/ doc links dangling, (4) 8 stale OL2r locks + auto_steal off + sentinel off, (5) 'crosslink intervene' documented but nonexistent (correct: crosslink issue intervene), (6) hooks not deployed, (7) completed-not-closed test issues accumulating.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: fix sandbox permission enforcement OR intentionally deny bash + update configs so agents use filesystem tools; then re-run the full 3-phase pipeline before declaring PASS.","created_at":"2026-08-01T00:11:14.940498841Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA1wGUB6nfMFgDfiYr+ZGxkK8sT+H7gRCOtEPQTeNxKACCwAqB