{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":422,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T01:18:21.508094060Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9dc62041-4dc2-4042-ac5d-724e6a2af5b4","comment_uuid":"b6eb4f48-2bbc-4881-936a-1a6d8a263aa8","author":"OL2r","content":"Evidence for the defect: (1) 'crosslink swarm reset' triggered sync.fetch() which rehydrated DB from stale hub -> dropped issues #5-#105 (recovered via compact); (2) repeated during this session — #78, #113, and #108 'not found' errors mid-wave, each requiring crosslink compact recovery; (3) Big Pickle Wave 0 review confirmed lock staleness misdetection is tied to the same heartbeat/hook deployment gap. Likely fix domain: sync.fetch() should reduce from own-ref events + checkpoint, not hydrate from a stale fetched hub; or the rehydration should refuse when local state is ahead. Investigate with #109.","created_at":"2026-08-01T01:18:21.502596301Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABABYa9rX+6CHuntTcYk7GhqPcyInPu+E1j6ThPGUbx4itV1vQP4s9CKpGhBvDtkLzVkihxGbpZdHNOhIXlyafrBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQB/MaGkmWltoN9tKfC3qZTyjl/3mWgOrCvGKfjXRbkTbsFNlyPkL0OakexpN7xvvPNYpXkBDIsSRQLmyYR5zOQI="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":423,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T01:19:23.100793453Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"87738dd2-98f2-495f-840b-2b7219d5d26e","comment_uuid":"246fda27-0b3b-49e7-91a6-20eb60e999fd","author":"OL2r","content":"ROOT CAUSE FOUND (investigation). The crosslink-guard.ts plugin — which contains the real permission enforcement (blocked git: push/rebase/reset/clean, gated git commit, DEFAULT_ALLOWED_BASH including cat/grep/find/pwd/echo) — EXISTS at .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts but is NOT LOADED. Root cause: .opencode/opencode.json has NO 'plugin' array (plugin: None, agent: []). Compare tripn-astro/.opencode/opencode.json which loads [orchestrator-guard, crosslink-guard, rtk-guard] and works. Without the guard, enforcement falls to opencode's built-in permission matcher, which mis-interprets the frontmatter bash map (denies git/ls/cat despite declaring allow; only 'crosslink *' passes) — exactly the defect Big Pickle reproduced live in 3 separate sessions.\n\nFIX DIRECTION (align-vs-deny): ALIGN — add the plugin array to .opencode/opencode.json loading crosslink-guard.ts (+ rtk-guard.ts if desired), restoring the intended enforcement. This is the ALIGN path (fix enforcement to match declared configs). SECURITY PAIRING required: with the guard loaded, its blocked-git list (push/rebase/reset/clean) + gated-commit logic restores the git-write blocker that today's blanket-deny coincidentally provided. Verify after load: read-only agents (reviewer/auditor) can run git status/log/diff/ls/cat, but git push/commit remain blocked per guard rules. This is the LOWER-RISK path vs deny-bash (which would require rewriting KICKOFF.md 'Always allowed' + git-based review section).","created_at":"2026-08-01T01:19:23.095357886Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAAB