{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":434,"timestamp":"2026-08-01T17:39:58.328629086Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"9dc62041-4dc2-4042-ac5d-724e6a2af5b4","comment_uuid":"bd596399-70b3-4e0b-b30f-49f4b25da19f","author":"OL2r","content":"ROOT CAUSE INVESTIGATED. Mechanism: sync_cmd -> fetch_v3 -> adopt_checkpoint_by_watermark (cache.rs: if remote_wm >= local_wm, overwrite local checkpoint with remote tip) -> hydrate_from_state. The hydration data-loss guard (hydration.rs:350) preserves SQLite-only rows ONLY when created_by IS NULL — but fork-created issues (create_issue_with_author) have created_by set, so they are NOT preserved when the reduced state omits them. Pre-#794, tracker_remote=origin (read-only) meant pushes 403'd and a stale remote checkpoint could be adopted with >= watermark while missing local-only events -> reduce omitted them -> hydration dropped them. FIXED IN PRACTICE by #794 (tracker_remote=fork): own-ref pushes succeed, remote checkpoint always covers local events, sync now hydrates non-destructively (verified 118/118). RESIDUAL CODE BUG to fix: the created_by IS NULL filter in hydrate_from_state is a latent data-loss trap for any SQLite-only row with non-null created_by. Recommended fix: preserve SQLite-only rows regardless of created_by (the filter looks like a legacy guard now wrong for fork-authored issues). Reopen/keep #119 for this code-level fix.","created_at":"2026-08-01T17:39:58.321622442Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAP/BZtNRcFx9qEX9JKJrj6bsg7rCfPml41M/jRM8FfzQ3GgpMKEAvZlnw9ms2DKjuM33/encnY189E1aE2Gp7Bw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZ