{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":468,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T01:13:49.632863877Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","title":"Crosslink hydration/sync state-integrity: multiple interrelated defects causing dropped or inconsistent issue state","description":"The hydration problem is broader than #119 alone. It is a family of interrelated state-integrity defects around sync/hydration/compaction, evidenced repeatedly this session and in prior work. Moving parts: (1) sync.fetch() rehydrates SQLite from stale hub state, dropping local-only issues/comments (#119 fixed the created_by filter, but the mid-session '#123 not found' + 'Issue not found' errors during concurrent kickoff launches show the residual race); (2) 0.9.0-beta.1 uuid-sync quirk: every sync/compact reverts issue UUIDs, breaking the hydration integrity check (see research-addenda/Research Addendum 03 - Crosslink 0.9.0-beta.1 uuid-sync bug.md); (3) worktree comments do not reach the hub until an explicit sync — observed with #120, #121, #123 reviewers (comments posted locally, invisible to the main DB until crosslink sync); (4) tracker_remote=fork vs origin hub-state consistency (#109 family); (5) no guard against concurrent kickoff launches each triggering their own hydration (the #123-not-found race). Recovery path has repeatedly been 'crosslink compact'. Open items: catalog all observed failure modes, reproduce each, and produce a consolidated fix or upstream report. Subissue: research-addenda document on the uuid-sync bug.","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ6mSEjFLyYt+PJ7dpnEtuDYXewkGxgLgo08S3YybaZxRgl4Um3U9XU3ciLxUyvhBNHMubKP+ckWAMYhkcCbfAU="}
