{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":472,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T01:18:48.218740740Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1acb2141-10eb-41ff-9005-5e15c6ae7525","comment_uuid":"06f3401e-2ad0-4859-b640-27b2a0182209","author":"OL2r","content":"INTEGRITY NOTE (2026-08-03): The second reviewer (mimo-v2.5, pp3g-UGdY) read the first reviewer's (gpt-5.6-luna, pp3g-4gKW) posted verdict via 'crosslink issue show 123' before writing its own — its verdict is NOT fully independent. Root cause: both reviewers were dispatched on the SAME issue thread, so the later arrival inherited the earlier verdict. The two verdicts converge (checkpoint comments + KICKOFF heartbeat; timeout-length is primary) but convergence is weakened by contamination. gpt-5.6-luna's verdict (01:07) is clean (first to post). Correct mechanism going forward: multi-reviewer dispatches MUST use per-reviewer isolated sub-issues so no reviewer can read another's output before completing its own; orchestrator synthesizes after all land. This rule is now part of this issue's spec and must be written into the playbook.","created_at":"2026-08-03T01:18:48.211592986Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAwxTEW2Lt+cmT+Hqy2wn25lFrwYrx3kzK87tFK1YybhjqKeoBQSIWVFr0U8KNPf4/RQ1zL8iSwkNmN4upE4tcCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPy4h82Yonq8ChMX+osHIlk1Wif1HUGskcaucpryNADtBYdEmRrvma9fAuNltMa2BlPY+5m4VWdzlE0kdZbhXwI="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":473,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T01:18:58.670356944Z","event":{"type":"IssueUpdated","uuid":"1acb2141-10eb-41ff-9005-5e15c6ae7525","description":"Update docs with timeout guidance + agent progress-feedback mechanism. Evidence: #120's 4-file fix took ~3 min real work on a 40m timeout; review/doc/port tasks all <=30m. 45m/40m/1h defaults overcommit and starve the operator of feedback. Deliverable: (1) timeout guidance in agent-orchestration-playbook.md + kickoff skill + SESSION-START (per-task-type guidance e.g. trivial <=10m, doc/simple 15-20m, port/multi-file 30m, review 15-20m; timeouts should be task-matched not fixed 1h); (2) a defined progress-feedback mechanism so agents report intermediate progress (e.g. mandatory checkpoint comments via crosslink issue comment --kind observation at milestones, periodic crosslink session action breadcrumbs, or a heartbeat/checkin step in KICKOFF.md template), so the operator never waits blind until timeout; (3) document in the same place the two-repo sync requirement: ASES and tripn-astro orchestrator roles must be updated together as one process; (4) REVIEWER-INDEPENDENCE RULE (added 2026-08-03 after a contamination incident): when dispatching MULTIPLE reviewers on the same question, each reviewer MUST post its verdict to its OWN isolated sub-issue (per-reviewer channels) so no reviewer can read another's verdict before completing its own; the orchestrator synthesizes after all verdicts land. Never dispatch multiple reviewers onto the same issue thread. Document this rule in the playbook so it cannot recur."},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOna2/+gWCTDHcyq8uPcUNq517AYFVcKKW75ThlqqoSW1ixAejHsNlpxLGbiNdLuQKAX35GwZ1/I15DvjkeSugA="}
