{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":489,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T02:54:33.300318793Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4b44cd8c-cd37-49fb-a645-0469be2fc61f","comment_uuid":"8991b791-c551-42be-8356-70faaa8bb344","author":"OL2r","content":"FINAL ALLOWLIST SPEC (2026-08-03) — synthesized from 3 independent reviewer verdicts (ling #128, big-pickle #130, nemotron #132; laguna #129 failed — silent provider hang) + operator decisions + thin-orchestrator token-budget principle.\n\nACCEPT (scoped): ps (targeted 'ps -o pid,etime,time,stat -p <pid>' form), pgrep, tmux (list-sessions / capture-pane with small scrollback -S -20 / display-message), grep (discipline: always pipe to head/tail), tail (bounded forms e.g. tail -50), head (bounded forms e.g. head -50), wc, stat, diff, free, df, which, date, uptime, env (discipline: selective 'env | grep FOO' only; NEVER paste raw output to shared channels), git worktree list (scoped), git -C (scoped read-only compact: status / log --oneline / diff --stat / show --stat), curl -I / curl --head only (headers, no body, no POST).\n\nACCEPTED WITH DELEGATION RULE: git log --oneline, git diff --stat, git show --stat (compact forms only; deep diff review = Reviewer's job).\n\nREJECT: find (mutation flags -delete/-exec), awk/sed (sed -i edits files), less (redundant with head/tail), blanket git log/diff/show (unbounded output), curl body/POST, any git write.\n\nNEW PLAYBOOK RULE (thin orchestrator): The orchestrator consumes bounded signals only. Any read requiring large volume (whole files, full diffs, log analysis) is DELEGATED to a subagent which returns a summary. Never paste large raw output into the orchestrator context or a shared channel. Rationale: orchestrator context is the scarcest resource; same principle as webfetch:deny on orchestrator while subagents have fetch.\n\nAPPLY TO BOTH REPOS (ASES + tripn-astro) per two-repo sync rule (playbook 5.5): .opencode/agents/orchestrator.md frontmatter bash map AND .crosslink/hook-config