{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":495,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T03:43:35.227603022Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"e17b7dd1-ee7c-4462-bf98-4dc7b28a11b5","title":"Research: background completion/notification mechanism when orchestrator dispatches subagents. Goal: when the orchestrator launches kickoff agents, the operator should be notified (or be able to check) without manual polling — we currently have NO proactive channel (operator must ask). Research: (1) crosslink sentinel (exists in hook-config, enabled:false — what can it do? completion notifications? dispatch-on-label only?); (2) opencode plugin system — tool.execute hooks, session events, can a plugin emit desktop/terminal notifications or post to a channel?; (3) existing opencode plugins/community solutions for agent-completion notification; (4) OS-level options (notify-send, terminal bell, systemd oneshot timers watching .kickoff-status). Deliverable: a recommendation for the cheapest reliable mechanism that closes the operator-blind-polling gap, with implementation sketch. Research via web fetch/search (granted for this subagent).","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBW7Cxg7IuD08GUXaPU8gaikfiv+DQrhL921PqpLbmW+N3F9nQZzDq+4egbrzXq6A1DnBsGMk8tkGtHUmO2vRAk="}
