{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":501,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:10:31.462469456Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"e17b7dd1-ee7c-4462-bf98-4dc7b28a11b5","comment_uuid":"3be014cf-ce79-4285-b6f6-d06b68869356","author":"OL2r","content":"REQUIREMENT CORRECTION (2026-08-03, operator): the monitoring goal is WORKING-vs-STALLED detection, not just completion notification. This reframes the recommendation: Path B (hook-notify, #134) and the completion-only options are INSUFFICIENT — a hung agent fires no hook and no notification. Required capability: continuous observation of .worktrees/*/.kickoff-status (state transitions LAUNCHING/RUNNING/DONE/FAILED + mtime staleness). Best-fit mechanisms: (a) systemd timer + Python watcher (#133 verdict) — 15-30s scan of status files + mtimes, emits on transition AND on staleness; (b) Path A sentinel local observer (#134) — poll-based, reuses notify pipeline, but sentinel disabled + 10-min latency. Both observe status files continuously. Recommend (a) as primary with staleness alerts; keep #134's Path A as the durable Rust option.","created_at":"2026-08-03T04:10:31.454999937Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABATRznQTDr2RbXSFXvGQwU/rMGmRlMZwsDJSYO0grqW6ftfJcOAYJknLJSblyJqS3D0SJ3+GJXrxrdJHxHbxPFAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQPUtmpQlLmVOXuKAaAEdthrKvzeH45tI40YXzpHjJNJ1l0NBl+p4itSe5nFdyiFf5h3FA2ynZCuqjnK750+3wgQ="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":502,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:10:41.030510407Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4b44cd8c-cd37-49fb-a645-0469be2fc61f","comment_uuid":"6fa24b11-e96e-430b-b3d6-5299bf3b1926","author":"OL2r","content":"STALL EVIDENCE (2026-08-03, orchestrator): opencode.log shows builder pp3g-YYRu's last internal activity at 02:59:22 (running Python verification script comparing bash maps across repos after editing both). Silence since — no further tool calls, no commit, no result comment. Same silent-hang signature as laguna (#129): mid-work then no output, zero errors logged. 30m timeout (started 02:55) expires ~03:25; if no commit by then, treat as failed per playbook empty-output rule and relaunch on a fresh agent.","created_at":"2026-08-03T04:10:41.023370394Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAiIKl1yqxfBhj2fhvtq8x/wUEmgQkNpTxxwn0y8eYskSENCDlo5mSmWo5DzIjR/Gus28tUh2wG5qYCaaa7j0JBA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEKuCXfSKXCUXAqvtCajFT8vZwMZJd48uFVwHcor8LV31nYNy+0zVfF3th0y8wFOU38dGDWbKa1iY4ql60Glmgk="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":503,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:25:20.038929813Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"246c7e5b-4bb4-404f-bfd3-d9eee60e0e3f","title":"Unified agent lifecycle watcher: monitoring + notification + automated stall recovery (one design incorporating #133/#134 research). PROBLEM: we have no proactive channel (operator must poll) AND a recurring failure mode (3x this session: laguna #129, YYRu #127, + historical) where a model request hangs silently — outgoing 'stream' never returns, no error, agent goes quiet. OBSERVABLE FINGERPRINT (per #123 two-signal rule): .kickoff-status not terminal + no activity (file mtimes / commits / comments) for >2x expected interval = STALLED. DESIGN — ONE background watcher (systemd timer + Python, zero-Rust per #133 verdict; sentinel extension as durable upgrade per #134 Path A) polling .worktrees/*/ every 15-60s, tracking per-agent state machine (LAUNCHING/RUNNING/DONE/FAILED/CI_FAILED + STALLED), and on state transition taking ACTIONS: (a) COMPLETED -> notify operator (desktop/webhook); (b) STALLED -> notify + PRESERVE WORK (commit uncommitted worktree changes to feature branch with [#N] ref) + kill tmux + RELAUNCH fresh agent on same issue with retry-handoff note (#115: prior attempt stalled at X, resume from committed state) + record recovery on issue (--kind observation); (c) FAILED -> notify + record. ESCALATION GUARD: max 2 auto-relaunches per issue, then STOP and notify operator (playbook HALT backstop; don't loop burning tokens). This DELIBERATELY DEVIATES from playbook 'HALT on failure, never auto-retry' — operator-approved policy direction, codify explicitly. RECONCILES with #133 (notification) + #134 (repurposing feasibility) + #115 (retry handoff) + #123 (two-signal rule). Deliverable: implementation sketch + policy doc; then build.","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrk