{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":514,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:38:40.512771735Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"246c7e5b-4bb4-404f-bfd3-d9eee60e0e3f","comment_uuid":"70691f81-ab3b-483f-8090-18995f380528","author":"OL2r","content":"TWO-TIER RECOVERY DESIGN (2026-08-03, operator + orchestrator): refine the STALLED action. Instead of kill+relaunch as the first response to a hung request, use a nudge-first approach because the hang is in the upstream request, not the agent's reasoning — the agent's context is intact, it just can't get a response. TIER 1 (preferred): request-level timeout on the opencode/provider client so a hung stream aborts and returns a retryable error to the agent loop (agent self-recovers; opencode already has AI_RetryError machinery — the gap is these requests apparently have no timeout configured). SUB-ITEM: research whether opencode supports configuring per-request timeouts, and how. TIER 2 (fallback): the watcher detects STALLED and first NUDGES the agent via tmux injection (e.g. 'tmux send-keys ... \"your last request timed out — continue\"'), waits one interval; only if no activity escalates to preserve-work + kill + relaunch (original STALLED action). Kill+relaunch becomes the LAST resort, not the first. The #133/#134 reviewers' options map to tiers: request-timeout = in-client; watcher-nudge = systemd-timer-with-injection; preserve+relaunch = escalation. UPDATE THIS ISSUE's deliverable: implementation sketch + policy doc covering both tiers.","created_at":"2026-08-03T04:38:40.504781418Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABArlH5ZBps09Pu8LY1RHyuyMXVlSBs8td6W83dijf+DVUTC0DBpu2dlUf0KeLELtiS4bZVqg+HmUv2nL7WpR2SBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMcmNGnZ12zPBudf2u0VKusyA6lThqjg75Wva4tVwheDKgSOBQKNIXQsRN8nd07OH2GKPlrTOq9OacevWpgqfQA="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":515,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:42:08.117120410Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"85bee50a-7e9b-4431-b63e-0ba2c0343595","comment_uuid":"1fb67684-efab-4246-bb33-dfe60594a795","author":"OL2r","content":"FOUND AND ASSESSED (2026-08-03): incident record located at /home/claude-code/projects/tripn-astro/.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/crosslink-db-rollback-incident.md (contributor 4Adb, 2026-08-02). SUMMARY: mid-session, crosslink issue DB reset to a June-era state; July/August issues (#338, #342, #370-376, #378) became 'not found' because they were LOCAL-ONLY (never pushed to hub) and a 'crosslink sync' re-hydrated SQLite from a stale hub checkpoint (June 9 baseline, watermark 2026-06-09, display_id_map empty). Repair flags can't resurrect what the hub doesn't know. No code lost — all work lives in git commits/branches. LESSONS: (1) don't run crosslink sync casually mid-session when local issues may be unpushed; (2) treat .kickoff-status flags as lies — check the issue comment trail before declaring stalled; (3) short review timeouts (a 1-file review took ~2 min; 30m too long); (4) model discipline (build=deepseek-v4-flash, review=mimo-v2.5); (5) prove serially then fan out, but don't fan out on an unstable tracker. ASSESSMENT: this is the SAME hydration/rollback failure family as ASES #125 (stale-hub rehydration dropping local-only issues) — both trace to sync.fetch() rehydrating from a stale hub checkpoint. The tripn-astro doc adds two lessons we should fold into #125/#126: the checkpoint watermark evidence (state.json next_display_id:1) and the 'flags are lies, check comment trail' detection rule. Recommend: copy this incident record into ASES docs (research/ or .crosslink/knowledge) and link it from #125 so both repos share the knowledge; do NOT duplicate the full text, reference it.","created_at":"2026-08-03T04:42:08.111036485Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABATDz11X5ONbQzYTLnoA+JKLZuDghAUWZ8lZHD5rrQitSkhPOzh455eMhw0gJU+sf6Ppd4GncVGhdC+pD8Q/uhBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMzL4sqlORuiWoG3yK+hHmZj78+DTK2EQiT+7esXNR/n62h5RXhi2z0q5xXZHBZuKn2xhAXorhzLqevIsnw85gc="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":516,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:42:20.363623727Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"4d6e75ae-d2b8-434d-9ae4-a92267450588","author":"OL2r","content":"CROSS-REFERENCE (2026-08-03): the tripn-astro crosslink-db-rollback-incident (2026-08-02, knowledge-cache doc) is the SAME failure family as this issue — sync.fetch() rehydrating SQLite from a stale hub checkpoint, dropping local-only issues (#338/#342/#370-376/#378 'not found' after a casual mid-session sync; hub checkpoint was June 9, watermark 2026-06-09, display_id_map empty). ASES observed the identical pattern all session (#123 not found, #124 not found, #137 not found on concurrent launches). Two extra lessons from the tripn-astro record worth folding into this issue's catalog: (1) the checkpoint state.json evidence pattern (next_display_id/watermark/display_id_map as the diagnostic), and (2) 'status flags are lies — check the comment trail before declaring stalled' (which matches our #127/#129 silent-hang evidence). Reference: /home/claude-code/projects/tripn-astro/.crosslink/.knowledge-cache/crosslink-db-rollback-incident.md. Consider consolidating into #126's doc catalog.","created_at":"2026-08-03T04:42:20.357149398Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAAGHixw5GOVv2r4tVKZ0LEhmymkfawcVGr2K/8mmxsbVH+t9KLFEbaSHhIo1Wba46IWzRpJt0T0tD3KRke81TAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJMGkTEhNoWpKZXXf6oIgPtETQ2qpAM48KgVC/8m+bouvLdliOJAIwgjzjCTGOBtp2q0FA/xwh4cdJvMplOsQwo="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":517,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:54:24.465992424Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"246c7e5b-4bb4-404f-bfd3-d9eee60e0e3f","comment_uuid":"cf898fbe-fee5-4161-9580-c845d739ad60","author":"OL2r","content":"REVISED DESIGN v2 (2026-08-03) — synthesized from two independent reviews: luna #136 (CONDITIONAL) + big-pickle #137 (directionally sound, structurally incomplete). Both independently converge on the same ship order and the same critical corrections.\n\nCONVERGENCE (strong signal):\n1. Tier 1 (request-level timeout) is the CORRECT root fix and the ONLY tier that actually fixes the observed hang. Implement via opencode provider config — the claude wrapper execs 'opencode run' so ALL kickoff agents are opencode; opencode 1.18.11 provider schema has timeout/headerTimeout/chunkTimeout (chunkTimeout aborts a hung SSE stream). NOTHING is configured today (verified). SUB-ITEM REQUIRED: experiment to verify post-abort behavior (does the agent loop get a retryable error and continue, or does the session die?) BEFORE building anything on it; measure typical chunk cadence to pick chunkTimeout values.\n2. Nudge-first is NOT recovery for a hung stream: tmux send-keys buffers while the client blocks (luna) and crosslink's built-in watchdog ALREADY implements the nudge and is INERT due to an exit-condition bug (big-pickle: launch.rs:88-89 exits when status file exists, but launch writes it before spawning watchdog). FIX the existing watchdog bug; nudge = cheap probe for idle-but-responsive agents, not hang recovery.\n3. Detection must use the HEARTBEAT file (.crosslink/.cache/last-heartbeat, 120s, already powers the watchdog) as PRIMARY signal — .kickoff-status mtime is static mid-run. Add debounce (2 consecutive detections), per-model silence floor from .kickoff-metadata.json timeout_secs, LAUNCHING grace, phase-adaptive deadlines. The 2x-expected-interval rule is an investigation trigger, NOT a destruction trigger.\n4. Completion edge (MUST FIX): finished-but-flagless agents (commit/result comment present, .kickoff-status missing DONE) = COMPLETED, not STALLED — else duplicate work on done issues (playbook 6.1: commit is ground truth).\n5. Systemic masking: >=2 stalls in a window = SYSTEMIC signal -> HALT, do NOT relaunch. Add cooldown/backoff, model/provider variation, per-issue token budget.\n6. Operational races: index.lock handling, coordination with kickoff cleanup, signing-key re-assertion (worktree may hold driver key), stale-lock handling for session work, watcher identity + mandatory sync-after-comment, persisted state machine (idempotent transitions on watcher restart).\n7. CI_FAILED policy: notify, do NOT auto-relaunch (code failure != hang).\n\nSHIP ORDER (both reviewers): PHASE 1 = monitor + notify + Tier 1 request-timeout config + retry-behavior experiment (non-destructive); PHASE 2 = fix existing watchdog bug + harden detection (heartbeat, debounce, floors); PHASE 3 = autonomous preserve+kill+relaunch with all gates, fault-injected, opt-in. Do NOT ship destructive tier until Phase 1 proven.\n\nDELIVERABLE UPDATE: implementation proceeds in phases; Phase 1 first (opencode config + watcher monitor/notify + experiment). Policy doc must codify the explicit HALT deviation + two-repo sync mirror to tripn-astro.","created_at":"2026-08-03T04:54:24.457275674Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAog5i8fbnN3VCXPubeMTUvOecwzMX3x1vFCNU5CIUL3cgZTnrOQHfra+wAVFZGCQXYq8t11Cy49hi+BsNjEysAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGRaMMNbrn17dZD9ehPMWK9az5ctZG/+TaA8n/oAE/kXjEHrSjxlb/