{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":523,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T04:59:01.129093977Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"246c7e5b-4bb4-404f-bfd3-d9eee60e0e3f","comment_uuid":"d577a56d-36b0-4f66-b59e-844f7399d1c9","author":"OL2r","content":"WORKFLOW RULE (2026-08-03, operator): when any kickoff/swarm agent is running, EVERY orchestrator turn MUST end with a brief Agent Status note covering each running agent (state, time-in, last signal) — even when there is nothing new to report. This keeps the operator informed without polling. To be codified in the playbook (agent-orchestration-playbook.md) alongside the checkpoint-comment contract.","created_at":"2026-08-03T04:59:01.119023169Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA5rIekiqZYxfVRNv9Mmlg1CTrfPNNsGtao5BjpUkgQz4XQDbGf7p1y4qqXoLdj9GZCI7tblogqmX/TEXvMgp8Cw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQA+TY1N4AllSHR187JXsSPAgQ37QM5CrNfg197YjLBLAOU2VR9aecNxQMZC7HhFNhx4wLg/ie0vkCh3bAXcqGQ0="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":524,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T05:05:19.532488249Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"246c7e5b-4bb4-404f-bfd3-d9eee60e0e3f","comment_uuid":"49adcef3-d259-47d5-a919-141df61b7548","author":"OL2r","content":"PHASE 1.5 ADDITION (2026-08-03) — from a live tripn-astro incident: reviewer completed (build PASS + full CHANGES REQUESTED review on #379) but the main-repo SQLite never re-hydrated from the hub, so 'issue show 379' showed empty output and the operator misdiagnosed failure. The dangerous 'fix' (main-repo crosslink sync) is the exact command that caused the June rollback (#338/#342/#370-376). LESSON: liveness (Phase 1 watcher) and data-visibility (hydration) are DIFFERENT failures; the watcher detects completion via .kickoff-status + heartbeat independent of the DB, but must NOT attempt to fix hydration divergence. PHASE 1.5: add OPTIONAL hydration-divergence reporting to the watcher status output — compare worktree/hub state vs main-repo DB and surface 'agent DONE but main DB stale — verify via hub' as a status line, WITHOUT auto-sync (too dangerous). The safe verification path (no sync): inspect refs/heads/crosslink/agents/<agent-id>/events.log on the hub ref for CommentAdded events. This incident reinforces #125 (hydration family) as the separate open item.","created_at":"2026-08-03T05:05:19.524945943Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAyLtw6IQtl7swy08KcANRWFVf58qZXmkSAwelLuVgWsp4IvlpKBILJD1cPKL5yYZAIKDapDnCZbcX0pV/GyX+CQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ6hXal9czHox8QSjWeBWCZUX0HAP5znk8Mdo96r