{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":529,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T05:20:09.615589661Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"179c7fab-c572-4486-9e51-7f8290d4dd37","title":"INFRA GAP: kickoff CLI hardcodes agent_type=None (no --agent flag) — all kickoff agents launch under default builder type regardless of role. Evidence: crosslink kickoff run --help has no --agent/--agent-type; src/commands/kickoff/mod.rs lines 95/285/370 all set 'agent_type: None'; run.rs:219-222 falls back to read_agent_type() from hook-config agent.type (default 'builder'). IMPACT: reviewer/auditor agents dispatched via kickoff run under the builder permission surface — role enforcement (by_type.reviewer/auditor git-write blocking) is NOT applied to kickoff-dispatched reviewers. Only swarm (phase_types) and the launch wrapper (--agent flag) can set role type. FIX: add an --agent-type CLI flag to kickoff run (types.rs already has agent_type field; wire it through mod.rs), or derive from issue labels. Note: this is the mechanism gap behind reviewer-independence concerns (#123 5.6) — reviewers are prompt-enforced read-only, not permission-enforced.","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMzPyAvCX0BDKCAIR11B9brrKMgF2+EhniRpIlWZ/5EcW9/+6L38JBzb/zN0+No9bsFqz6aNno5I5nna9GcAdAw="}
