{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":532,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T05:20:33.467446328Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f07207cd-d69f-4856-93e4-7db9b3d7a922","title":"DOC UPDATE: free-model failures are NOT always rate limits — check the opencode log for the 429/error signature before assuming. Evidence (2026-08-03, #129 laguna incident): the 'stalled' laguna reviewer had ZERO level=ERROR entries in its session log (ses_03aa886c0ffeXKFRLMhDrbTNyd) — last event was an outgoing 'message=stream' request at 02:01:30 that never completed, no error. Compare: historical laguna rate-limit incidents (July 23-26) all logged 'Provider rate limit exceeded'. Ling + big-pickle + nemotron completed fine in the same window. CONCLUSION: laguna's freeze was a silent provider-side hang, NOT a rate limit. UPDATE .crosslink/knowledge/model-discipline.md: add the failure-discrimination rule — on a stalled free/paid agent, check ~/.local/share/opencode/log/opencode.log for the error signature; rate limit = 'Provider rate limit exceeded' / 429; hang = outgoing stream with no response and no error. Do not assume rate limits hit all free models at once.","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQETU4WRUpSERi//4Rmyx/A1wyh7uCSnvjb5iUQx6SwKBV8aPp9Y7X5dJEWwQs32wpCLszoSK5KIvyRSbKOXsSQY="}
