{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":550,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T06:22:31.347469991Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"246c7e5b-4bb4-404f-bfd3-d9eee60e0e3f","comment_uuid":"b5864079-ab56-4cdb-960b-b80734e81ac3","author":"OL2r","content":"PHASE 1.5 REFINEMENT (2026-08-03, operator + orchestrator): the watcher status output should be COMPACT-BY-DEFAULT, full-pane-ON-DEMAND — per the thin-orchestrator principle (#127). Routine check = tail of pane (~5 lines: current action) + pane-motion (changed since last check) + .kickoff-status/heartbeat/mtime; NOT the full pane. Full pane content is only fetched when adjudicating a stall (where-did-it-stop determines wait vs nudge vs kill+relaunch). The watcher's notify/status line should be one compact line per agent (state, time-in, last-action, pane-tail); full tmux capture-pane is an opt-in detail for stall investigation. Rationale: full panes are token-expensive noise for routine checks; compact signals are sufficient and cheaper (see also #127 thin-orchestrator rule).","created_at":"2026-08-03T06:22:31.340270751Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAJMiXjz9XfAHYQJ8WCVBg2Upm92tjKgHXATo+S7nn5irOpT7BmchXPyk6IeUFFqgto6riSWitdnLEEazFGpYdDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMOPKnrjrmBwA6bc43Y3Zmq1z525mPrM5MGDlDNFxu60UQXXWxkEz6d3q+BhJxlLat6J6hBemiYzousCNoc+4gA="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":551,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T06:32:41.341384877Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d4822b37-51ef-4159-a754-5c78bb90dbdd","title":"LATER: evaluate opencode time-context caching plugin (proposal from opencode community). Removes 'Today's date' from the system prompt (via experimental.chat.system.transform) and injects a timestamp <system-reminder> on the last user message (experimental.chat.messages.transform), improving prompt-cache hits by making the system prompt static. NOT related to current work (hang/stall recovery); deliberately deferred. Concerns to evaluate when revisited: (1) experimental.chat.* API is version-fragile (we're on opencode 1.18.11); (2) reminder timestamp is itself dynamic, may partially self-defeat cache reuse; (3) mutates conversation content (part.text +=); (4) it does NOT address request-timeout/stall issues — those are handled by chunkTimeout + watcher (#135). Also tracked separately: the ESC/interrupt failure (could not interrupt an agent through the tmux/systemd-run/wrapper stack) — diagnose that as its own item.","priority":"low","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLk6OSW9z2EQL2pMvVIJ9fx6+fRGA7VBJbtjDE45tITa/YHPkUxVF2gwoGZeZznNcHR9d0JBcMTbyrgVbsPWaA4="}
