{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":556,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T17:34:40.896006564Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"951b3b57-44f1-4503-9404-6cb182065dd1","title":"URGENT Tier-1 experiment (from #135 Phase 1 follow-up): verify whether the opencode provider request-timeout config actually catches the silent-hang failure. EVIDENCE: two NEW hangs today (pp3g-K6yV #138, pp3g-OZWZ #142) occurred AFTER the chunkTimeout config was merged + restart (~05:3x). Both showed the identical signature: last outgoing 'stream' never returns, zero ERROR entries, process stays alive, pane freezes. If chunkTimeout was active in those launches, it did NOT prevent the hang — OR the config wasn't actually applied to kickoff-launched agents. EXPERIMENT: (1) confirm the config is present and active for kickoff agent launches (check ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json is read by the launched opencode process — verify env/config propagation through the claude wrapper + tmux/systemd-run); (2) deliberately reproduce a hang or observe whether a hung stream aborts within chunkTimeout (300s) and what the agent loop does afterward (retryable error vs session death); (3) check whether the opencode-go provider even honors chunkTimeout (provider-side semantics). Deliverable: definitive answer — does the current config protect against this failure, and if not, what does (client-side abort, provider knob, or watcher nudge). Read-only investigation + possibly a controlled minimal test. Feeds #135 Phase 1 completion.","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGV5wzVAcNgJq4OHxyS5/XvedGSW7cE8+CaGczDT22iShGOa85FYOOPlECWYnAJKMdVxe47mpghvHWkXgA2awg0="}
