{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":559,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T17:47:02.194579712Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"951b3b57-44f1-4503-9404-6cb182065dd1","comment_uuid":"db73f813-8804-4a76-a9b6-dda5b98158a2","author":"OL2r","content":"SCOPE ADDITION (2026-08-03): FOLD-IN — investigate enforcing the 'orchestrator ends every turn with an Agent Status note' workflow rule via an opencode plugin hook, not conversational discipline. Proposed mechanism: a plugin (in the orchestrator session, alongside crosslink-guard) hooks 'session.idle' (the turn-ended signal — fires when the model finishes responding; NOT tool.execute.* which is mid-turn); on idle, query crosslink for running agents (crosslink kickoff list) and if any run and no status was recorded this turn, inject/emit a reminder or append the status. COMPLEMENTARY to the #135 watcher (which notifies the OPERATOR via notify-send/webhook); this enforces ORCHESTRATOR discipline. UNVERIFIED questions for #144 to answer while investigating opencode 1.18.11 plugin surface: (1) can a session.idle handler MUTATE/append the assistant response, or only emit a separate notification? (2) confirm plugins run in the orchestrator session (crosslink-guard already does — but verify session.idle availability + timing); (3) design a simple 'status recorded this turn' state flag. If mutation is unsupported, recommend the fallback (reminder emission) or an alternative enforcement point.","created_at":"2026-08-03T17:47:02.186177619Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAIzN0pwrxUHOeykRupNPbYrQ/IqJIthaN/elqLLmarQyC9HKgU3wVNtgP5i1Pcb8rgIYerCefG2Z7mO4Et3+ZBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO