{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":560,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T17:52:43.459646685Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"b98e733b-7a1f-4842-815b-51e3801b021f","author":"OL2r","content":"CONSOLIDATED STATE-OF-KNOWLEDGE (2026-08-03) — current understanding of the hydration family, for #126 catalog reference:\n\nCORE MECHANISM (confirmed): crosslink sync re-hydrates the local SQLite DB from the hub state; when the hub/hub-cache is stale, local-only issues are dropped or remapped. Local DB is a projection; hub is supposed to be source of truth; sync path has no safe guard for 'local ahead of hub'.\n\nOBSERVED FAILURE MODES (5+ instances):\n1. June-era rollback — stale hub checkpoint (June 9, next_display_id:1) + casual sync -> #338/#342/#370-376/#378 'not found' (tripn-astro 2026-08-02)\n2. Mid-session 'not found' drops on concurrent kickoff launches (#123/#124/#137) — each launch triggers own hydration, racing (ASES this session)\n3. Worktree comments invisible until explicit sync — agent posts review locally, main DB doesn't see (tripn-astro #379 misdiagnosis)\n4. uuid-sync quirk — sync/compact reverts issue UUIDs, breaking hydration integrity check (0.9.0-beta.1, Research Addendum 03)\n5. Display-id collision — 4 local-only issues collided with hub ids [1,2,3,4], remapped to negative local ids (ASES 2026-08-03)\n\nROOT-CAUSE THREADS:\n- #119 fixed the created_by IS NULL filter defect (code-level trap) + regression test. Family persists — operational stale-hub-sync hazard unaddressed.\n- Hub-cache wrong-ref suspicion (tripn-astro -hub-cache/ HEAD = refs/heads/crosslink/hub, stale, not current checkpoint) — UNVERIFIED, #142 stalled before verdict.\n- No guard against concurrent hydration (race, no lock/serialization).\n\nOPERATIONAL MITIGATIONS (codified):\n- Hub agent refs are ground truth; verify via git show refs/heads/crosslink/agents/<id>/events.log, never blind sync (playbook 6.5)\n- Never run crosslink sync in main repo to 'refresh' visibility — rollback trigger\n- #126 doc catalog consolidates all evidence\n\nNEW DATA POINT (2026-08-03): tripn-astro DB recovery via 'crosslink compact' WORKED — fixed the read path per the playbook, DB restored. Compact is the validated safe recovery path (vs blind sync). Add to #126 recovery-path evidence.\n\nOPEN: definitive mechanism answer (which ref does hydration read) pending #144; consolidated root-cause fix (safe re-hydration guard / config knob / checkpoint re-point) still open.","created_at":"2026-08-03T17:52:43.452972592Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAEt3DtLQNstQeNlw7p6jYe3SAdu8x3DhyuVxfWH00+MZXhxxJ5mYkx2aKE/UIz2Hxi56lvtEJgEAyUgzGSSfbDg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGd4fE3HFeYtLOfrNu4hWsvhIUagwmqRKFZ36vDKvabf+ei1i/+SRHrVZ0uf5gqKVD7cSkp2TW4tbCeIFK6ugQc="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":561,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:14:00.693876735Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7fea5a54-4818-403e-a458-b39204695bbf","title":"FORK/UPSTREAM FIX: patch opencode wrapSSE to remove the text/event-stream content-type guard so chunkTimeout covers ALL response bodies. Evidence (#144 verdict): wrapSSE in packages/opencode/src/provider/provider.ts (v1.18.11) returns the response UNWRAPPED when content-type lacks text/event-stream — chunkTimeout is a no-op, and the overall timeout (AbortSignal.timeout) fails to abort the already-resolved body read. Result: non-SSE responses hang forever, zero ERROR, flags lie as RUNNING — the exact signature of today's 3 hangs (laguna #129, K6yV #138, OZWZ #142). FIX: remove/relax the content-type guard, or add a general body-read deadline, so chunkTimeout applies to all response bodies regardless of content-type. This is an opencode SOURCE change (config alone cannot fix it — proven by #144's controlled reproduction). If upstream opencode won't accept, it's a fork patch. VERIFY: controlled hang test with application/json content-type must now abort within chunkTimeout. PREREQUISITE STATUS: none — independent of #135 watcher work. Blocked-by/related: #144 (verdict), #135 (watcher).","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMy9TU9fRgNh7DyDf44WeKXi8enzUST1LUdUUU74ltmMOxq4/gomqJfTIFBctFwojpfEm9/h3t+cnXMT1E0RDAQ="}
