{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":564,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:14:25.726030581Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"72d9de98-a7f4-443d-ac77-46a2ad6eb355","title":"UPGRADE #135 watcher Phase 3: change recovery from NUDGE to KILL-AND-RESTART after N stale checks. Evidence (#144 verdict + #138/#142 hang): the current watchdog (launch.rs build_watchdog_script) sends tmux send-keys 'continue working' up to max_nudges=5 — but a hung stream promise cannot be unblocked by keystrokes; the agent only reads them after the stream returns (which never happens). Nudge is useless for this failure mode. FIX: after heartbeat staleness exceeds a threshold, KILL the tmux session + relaunch a fresh agent on the same issue with retry-handoff note (#115), preserving work first (commit uncommitted changes). This is the #135 Phase 3 destructive tier — gate it per the reviewers' criteria (luna #136, big-pickle #137): heartbeat-primary detection with debounce, commit-ground-truth completion edge, systemic-correlation HALT (>=2 stalls in window), cooldown/backoff, model variation, token budget. ALSO note: with the #145 wrapSSE patch, hangs should become rare, making kill/restart a last-resort safety net rather than the primary path. PREREQUISITE: #138 (watchdog fix) landed (preserved commit 799ce67); #145 (wrapSSE) reduces hang frequency. Related: #135, #144, #138, #115.","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNGPvKNHaw/e8XeznGAIaRfwVBtFepYKDk68a+4ZF5s+6lYC8ueeQ+EWmiCxA1VV3xcPalnn7gxpIOEzV9cR5A0="}
