{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":571,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:28:35.852370182Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2ccb5763-6072-4a50-b949-8343c776c580","title":"DESIGN/RESEARCH: evaluate crosslink blocking-dispatch (kickoff run --wait) + inline pane surfacing, informed by opencode Task-tool UX. MOTIVATION (operator): opencode's Task tool already has the UX we built from scratch — in-the-loop dispatch, inline tmux-pane visibility (click running agents to see panes), native timeout/abort. Crosslink kickoff is fully async + detached (worktree/hub/isolation) which is why we needed the #135 watcher + status notes + kill/restart. GOAL: borrow Task-tool UX WITHOUT losing crosslink durability. OPTIONS: (A) opencode plugin surfacing running crosslink agents (poll .worktrees/*/, show live pane tail + state) — depends on whether opencode plugins can render interactive UI or only emit status (related to session.idle fold-in #144); (B) crosslink 'kickoff run --wait' blocking mode — streams the agent's tmux pane until completion/timeout, replicating Task-tool semantics while keeping worktree/hub; (C) hybrid — Task tool for quick watchable work, crosslink for durable/parallel, plugin bridge for inline visibility. DELIVERABLE: feasibility assessment against opencode 1.18.11 plugin API + crosslink fork source (where --wait would live), recommended path (my lean: B), implementation sketch. Research/design task — flash model.","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLxMi0N1kbokQTXLdDE9Q2X27+AljwxVWZ7/HsRLqHDk+sQYFlCchgdpEyOuyOu5JLKGfWl/oo8UmQBC6qArRQ0="}
