{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":574,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T18:32:07.581489241Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7fea5a54-4818-403e-a458-b39204695bbf","comment_uuid":"a39d9009-8ede-402b-98e9-7bd3dc41c0f1","author":"OL2r","content":"DECISION + UPSTREAM REFS (2026-08-03): #145 is a DUPLICATE at root-cause level per #147 research — NOT novel. Reference these upstream reports when filing/commenting: (1) PR #39516 (draft, Jul 29) — chunkTimeout only wraps text/event-stream; proposes wrapping every streamed response body; linked issue #31122 (LLM stream deadlock); (2) issue #26487 (May 9) — same wrapSSE guard; Bedrock application/vnd.amazon.eventstream bypasses chunkTimeout; proposes removing/expanding the guard; (3) PR #35743 (open) — eventstream matching + per-provider content-type allowlisting; (4) issue #39968 — chunkTimeout only watches raw bytes, misses parsed-stream stalls (9.5h half-open stream); (5) issues #37580, #36739, #40205 (v1.18.11 opencode-go freeze — our version), #40065. OUR ADDED VALUE: controlled reproduction (fake hanging server, application/json content-type) proving any non-SSE response hangs indefinitely with zero-error RUNNING symptom — file as a comment/variant on #39516/#26487 per repo submission guidelines. DECISION (operator): PATCH LOCALLY — upstream PRs are open/draft with unknown fix timeline; we cannot wait. Local patch = remove/relax the wrapSSE content-type guard in our installed opencode (source change), verify with the controlled hang test, and document the divergence from upstream (same pattern as crosslink fork). Do NOT file a new duplicate issue; contribute our reproduction to the existing reports instead.","created_at":"2026-08-03T18:32:07.566814139Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAlD3dWesPw