{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":589,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:28:20.358100922Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"c212e3bd-e79a-41b0-bd0b-679d4b8c3b83","title":"DURABLE FIX for the opencode silent-hang issue (supersedes the interim binary patch in #145). Context: #144 proved non-SSE responses bypass chunkTimeout (wrapSSE content-type guard) causing silent infinite hangs; #145 applied an emergency same-length binary patch (if(false)return) that stops the permanent hang but (per 4-reviewer consensus #150/#151/#152/#153) is EPHEMERAL and does not fix the silent retry loop. DURABLE SOLUTION: (1) SOURCE REBUILD — pin a fork of sst/opencode @ v1.18.11, apply the one-line provider.ts patch (remove/relax the text/event-stream content-type guard so chunkTimeout wraps all bodies), bun build, replace opencode.exe; document so the fix survives opencode upgrade. (2) DISTINCT NON-SSE DEADLINE — instead of reusing chunkTimeout for all bodies, add a longer body-completion deadline for non-SSE responses (preserves original intent of not aborting slow-but-legitimate non-streaming bodies; hy3 F2). (3) ERROR SURFACING + RETRY BUDGET — make chunkTimeout abort produce a visible retryable error and cap retries (currently zero ERROR entries + silent infinite retry loop; the real root cause per all reviewers). (4) VERIFY — ctl.abort() is per-request not shared (hy3 F4); test a slow-but-legitimate non-SSE body. FEEDS: #135 watcher kill/restart (#146) remains the recovery safety net. Related: #144, #145, #146, #135.","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAKELGuuIi+mQm/8fhLQY3KOaX87zhpwi+VsnaGSHgzXU9rZ8aJE+6nNcuPRrbIXWV80MAEU55k3oRYL8KRwOgQ="}
