{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":601,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T21:35:45.834834444Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2d237d66-4428-4d53-a565-b790def3cfa7","title":"RESEARCH: tool to expose a CACHE-HIT PERCENTAGE counter for the conversation + subagent dispatches, so token consumption is monitored accurately. MOTIVATION: we currently cannot see prompt-cache hit rate during a session or across subagent dispatches — important for cost tracking (cache hits are much cheaper than misses) and for validating cache-related changes (e.g. the #143 time-context caching plugin idea). REFERENCE: CodeWhale has this feature (cache hit percentage display) — research how they surface it. Also note: this harness-evaluation tooling will itself be part of the HARNESS RESEARCH PROJECT at a future date (tracked elsewhere). DELIVERABLE: survey available options (opencode built-in? provider API usage telemetry? models.dev/opencode-go API cache headers? CodeWhale approach; a plugin that logs cache-hit headers per request), recommend the cheapest reliable counter, implementation sketch. Research task — flash model per routing rule. Low priority (deferred until after the reliability frontier).","priority":"low","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQLqjHjGfMP5/jkckox7TAVQM3oDbkSJcwcbY4dQKt95qOld69lLtBOIvv9/86uMbcismTMFO2UEEjPty4oCygwQ="}
