{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":639,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T22:52:48.353262225Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"4634e7fb-e5bc-47ea-8c85-d3190501cc15","comment_uuid":"e8838d02-1c4c-4a4a-a2a2-f9d26505b599","author":"OL2r","content":"RESEARCH LINK (2026-08-03): today's reliability work is a live instance of the lifecycle-ownership question this issue tracks. The silent-hang failure family (#144/#145/#154/#146) exposed that AGENT LIFECYCLE STATE (who owns it, who recovers it, what observes it) is a real operational problem at the tooling layer — mirroring the statechart-vs-engine tension the execution-engine-ui synthesis flagged (statechart owns lifecycle; engine only schedules). Observations transferable: (a) nudge cannot unblock a hung stream — recovery requires kill/restart (ownership of the recovery action); (b) status flags lie — an independent observer (watcher/heartbeat) is needed for ground truth; (c) lifecycle recovery must preserve work + retry-handoff, not restart blind. These are evidence for how the Execution Engine's lifecycle-management role must behave. See #135 (watcher), #154 (durable fix), #146 (kill/restart), #125 (hydration state integrity).","created_at":"2026-08-03T22:52:48.346281935Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAHvb5XRyUgeyxmtEre3d22j33VtM6zVLeoDMChvusZ47g32KreP/mNQg8NAMQuk2xU5C9nB/zCL9mVYc+jQCSBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCJsKwEz3bggweMgGI0vTAES3cGCqzqhTtm6TG5AuFyPeRCq6TIrnmgF8nfghYlXOtxqqQhVd1v2IpxdaKTM/Qo="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":640,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T22:53:00.624233351Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"1a24fd47-590c-44a4-b9ba-91d91355affe","comment_uuid":"326d2925-312b-4540-85bd-a3c5b0e254d2","author":"OL2r","content":"RESEARCH LINK (2026-08-03): provenance granularity for agent records — today's reliability work provides evidence. The silent-hang failure family showed that AGENT OUTPUT RECORDS need provenance at the level of: which agent/session produced it, whether it was observed at the hub vs local DB (hub-refs ground truth, #125), and what state the agent was in when produced (flags lie; heartbeat/comment-trail is ground truth, #123/#140). The fork-history audit (#160) also showed commit provenance matters (rebase vs cherry-pick of identical patches — patch-ids preserve identity across history rewrites). These are concrete granularity requirements for provenance in the Execution Engine. See #125 (hydration/state integrity), #160 (fork provenance), #135 (watcher observation).","created_at":"2026-08-03T22:53:00.617914459Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAbnugBwj1b1GNwpj8+tolxArzjzFPdQzIUJELz63t9E3b5SknQfbhzDZOqb2Cgn8ovfBS/p6wKA9zZ+ZUVkhUCg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNl9WDmNPNDfzhEf06lN9YS6J/IopHqCk7/oHNSPHwuRyuxG0UaLZ9Vm3upOo9HPdvu7ZnLCRaK1fMBjScqPhQI="}
