{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":659,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T23:44:36.407754507Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"27980834-49cb-45ce-943c-f01b6ef92132","author":"OL2r","content":"LOCK DESIGN FINDING (2026-08-03, code-verified): locks are NOT fulfilling their blocking purpose due to two gaps. (1) The crosslink-guard plugin (crosslink-guard.ts) NEVER consults the lock table — its active-issue gate reads .active-issue sentinel + session status only; zero references to the lock table. So agent tool calls proceed on issues the lock table says are held by another identity (e.g. OL2r). (2) session work DOES enforce locks (src/commands/session.rs:246-259: enforce_lock + try_claim_lock; bails with 'Lock on #N was claimed by X' if another agent holds it) — but the STALE-detection path makes it bypassable (steal succeeds, or warn-and-proceed when holder looks stale). Root reason staleness can't be trusted: heartbeat hooks not deployed in worktrees (#135 Phase 2 item), so the code defaults to warn-not-block rather than risk blocking a live agent. CONCEPTUAL ISSUE (operator): a lock should BLOCK — currently it warns instead, so it isn't fulfilling its purpose. FIX ORDER: (1) make staleness reliable (deploy heartbeat into worktrees, #135 Ph2) so locks can confidently block/auto-steal; (2) wire the lock table into the crosslink-guard plugin (separate subissue) so the tool gate also respects held locks. Also noted: 18 stale OL2r locks currently — driver-identity locks never released, a cleanup gap. Related: #135, #160, #146.","created_at":"2026-08-03T23:44:36.398350308Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAir3F0VQN04J9Q/O5mX/GXKp27ZjQA/s6z/aimb5+P7uVr5ovx22wna+7KZN1H+obQOuukYainvwlM4zk4gSfCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFUG7StC+Ai+HDKnbVCzFVUKbOZxI/K5JSQ6mgb8M2HtpM2AvqjxAKUHnNJgHLjDRkSwLIF/FMc3dVWqh1rVlgU="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":660,"timestamp":"2026-08-03T23:44:49.624678213Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"0f511f63-230d-4593-a201-9b3a7c87b0c6","title":"FIX: wire the crosslink lock table into the crosslink-guard plugin so locks actually block","description":"CODE FINDING (#125, 2026-08-03): crosslink-guard.ts (the plugin that gates agent tool calls) never consults the lock table — its active-issue gate reads .active-issue sentinel + session status only. Result: agent tool calls proceed on issues the lock table says are held by another identity (e.g. OL2r); locks only 'warn' and are bypassable via staleness-steal. A lock's purpose is to BLOCK; it is not fulfilling that purpose at the plugin layer. FIX: wire the lock table into crosslink-guard.ts so the tool gate respects held locks (block writes/bash on an issue whose lock is held by another live identity). PREREQUISITE (order matters): make staleness detection reliable FIRST — deploy heartbeat hooks into worktrees (#135 Phase 2) — otherwise hard-blocking on 'held' locks will false-block live agents when staleness is misdetected (the very reason the code currently defaults to warn). Deliverable: plugin reads lock state (via crosslink locks list or direct DB), blocks when lock held-and-fresh, allows when stale/absent; verify no false blocks on live agents; test the steal path. Related: #125 (finding), #135 (heartbeat prerequisite), #146 (kill/restart), #160 (lock staleness observed).","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIToZn+yAu2TCZS3JoxMhlA9XydQiLZigywk6yi83CR7sRlgarItI0ARTB8+Alw08AIksR1qE+7BvB/5RfZgeww="}
