{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":694,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T00:43:29.711558852Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"fbd70c07-aa31-4974-8f85-5d1129d40e0d","title":"INTAKE: live-localhost verification convention from tripn-astro combined-verify-server retrospective. Source: /home/claude-code/projects/tripn-astro/docs/combined-verify-server-retrospective.md (2026-08-04, 3.7KB). SUMMARY: for visually verifying multi-site/multi-page changes during updates, DON'T use per-site 'astro dev' (HMR fragile across disconnects, base-path confusion, blank-404 traps). INSTEAD: build once into a combined dist (scripts/build-combined.mjs assembles all sites into subpaths), serve with python3 -m http.server in a tmux session on localhost:8080, operator clicks through real production URLs, batches design notes, builder rebuilds (~30s) per round. Key lessons: tmux not bare backgrounding (Bash tool kills background procs); check base paths (wrong URL = blank 404); verify combined build assembled all subfolders before serving. ACTION: (1) copy the retrospective into ASES docs (docs/research/ or docs/standards/ — decide home); (2) file as a reusable convention; (3) derive crosslink issues for a future session (document the convention in playbook/tooling; consider a reusable script/checklist; apply to ASES verification workflows).","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF+oJH7dvJEtbqnuUqmDNUZpSx5dgcv2m2tES8/UQyIlKtOVIxdEEJHraaB/fvXpoVtzoAEtFIKF5BB9q2XRNQg="}
