{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":707,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T00:55:48.651203265Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"92ee214c-d937-494e-8006-600dfe5b04c7","author":"OL2r","content":"SYSTEMIC DRIFT FINDING (2026-08-04): multiple agents today have DRIFTED into the V3-lock/hydration internals instead of their assigned tasks — big-pickle (#149 review), #160 fork agent, #163 audit agent, #168 intake agent. Root cause hypothesis: every 'crosslink session work' emits a stale-lock warning (OL2r holds, steal doesn't persist due to pre-31a3e2e8 binary), and agents keep deciding to INVESTIGATE the lock mechanics rather than push past the warning. This wastes their time budget and produces scope drift. MITIGATION (already being applied): tightly-scoped prompts + 'ignore the lock warning, proceed with the deliverable' instruction; early kill on drift. LONG-TERM: the lock bug (#166 V3 fix + #167 plugin wiring) removes the recurring warning that triggers the drift. Worth a playbook note: agents must treat stale-lock warnings as non-blocking noise and proceed with the task.","created_at":"2026-08-04T00:55:48.643363371Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABALtVRycQAXMOfa2S2TrKMun0KlBrb9GGpwbTOFdfo0b/xUhy10S0k+hHBM6SXFFMbdGJ2fouYhumy8DkauJBjBw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAHhvFl5QV+TpQi9wqkEe2IhPnrbEG70RpuMt8lFpqkGwtUXj28EiWx3elHtAGhkzCYqQR3eZjZ1zieqNAaLmQw="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":708,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T01:38:26.668634059Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"938b926a-c400-4088-837f-9bc1322dd8d7","comment_uuid":"5a5d854c-7eb7-4fc5-8cc7-744cf6891d14","author":"OL2r","content":"PROVISIONAL DECISION (2026-08-04, operator): adopt OPTION A — use existing crosslink surfaces as the orchestrator's markdown path (crosslink knowledge add/edit, crosslink issue comment, crosslink session end --notes); ZERO new code. Rationale: it works today, keeps the write path inside crosslink (narrow/auditable/sync-aware), and avoids a fork change. If it proves insufficient in practice (e.g. need dated repo-file notes), revisit option B ('crosslink note' command) — recorded as part of the project's continual learning. The SESSION-END convention is being written on this assumption (see the SESSION-END doc + decision trail).","created_at":"2026-08-04T01:38:26.660607718Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAR3+1ltVHv3zpcjcDEILxK/bTpsetd8rQQ8Yia/p0jOJ/5QYNXa8KXyWyk/yDTgT4glHXfcuuIu5Wy81QsgajBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQH8UGtS94GvS8AmW71ysI/wTlsNZqeQPWXVDuU9QwT7jTZ8l9R0yKE/LNPjtDYIaZR6P38wrlVCqdWopfMTXAA0="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":709,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T01:46:25.500820068Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"cae9ce6e-e13e-493b-8fb1-528ff2aa5af2","title":"BUG: orchestrator git merge is gated in by_type but blocked by root blocked_git_commands when the by_type override isn't applied. Evidence (2026-08-04): hook-config.json by_type.orchestrator gated_git_commands = [git commit, git merge] and its blocked list OMITS merge; but the ROOT-level blocked_git_commands (line 15-19) INCLUDES 'git merge'. crosslink-guard.ts applies the by_type override only when CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE env is set or resolveAgentType() resolves to orchestrator; if the override is missed (env not exported, worktree hook-config stale, resolveAgentType fallback), the root blocked list wins and merge is hard-blocked ('human performs all git write operations') despite the config gating it. IMPACT: orchestrator merge capability is UNRELIABLE — works only when by_type loads. This also explains the earlier confusion where the agent said merge was gated but the plugin blocked it. FIX OPTIONS: (1) remove 'git merge' from the ROOT blocked list (it's gated per-role anyway, roles that must not merge (reviewer/auditor) already block it in their by_type); (2) make applyAgentTypeOverride fail-closed (log loudly when it can't resolve the type). RECOMMEND (1) + (2). Related: #167 (lock plugin wiring), #125 (hydration/config consistency), #121 (orchestrator role).","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJQucSKUGemcpJTEDA0kiLpLGVWAqBbohLndoocGcm39+7TLyz6npnF+4Isrxx2g6lc/mu1tIZu1UU8DLNZqKwc="}
