{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":725,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T03:51:21.408521100Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"cae9ce6e-e13e-493b-8fb1-528ff2aa5af2","comment_uuid":"37f0c503-8212-4f45-818f-b8c30c6adbe8","author":"OL2r","content":"## Review Summary: PASS (no blocking findings)\n\nReviewed commit 17a1960e125d7b6ba54a8024ff322b0fa5965746 for issue #173 (orchestrator git-merge gating). Read-only adversarial review; no writes performed.\n\n### Step 1 — Commit scope: PASS\n- 'git show 17a1960 --stat' shows exactly 2 files: .crosslink/hook-config.json (1 insertion removed) and .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts (+27/-3). No scratch files, no .crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref in the commit.\n- Working tree has an uncommitted .last-hydrated-ref change (ref-hash auto-hydration churn, not part of this commit; harmless).\n\n### Step 2 — hook-config.json: PASS\n- JSON valid: 'crosslink workflow diff' loaded the file without parse error (python3/node not executable under this reviewer sandbox's bash policy; validated via the CLI loader + full-file read).\n- Root-level blocked_git_commands (lines 179-194) does NOT contain 'git merge' and still contains git push, git rebase, git cherry-pick, git reset, git checkout ., git restore ., git clean, git stash, git tag, git am, git apply, git branch -d, git branch -D, git branch -m.\n- agent_overrides.blocked_git_commands still contains 'git merge' (line 19); by_type.reviewer.blocked_git_commands contains it (line 75); by_type.auditor.blocked_git_commands contains it (line 102).\n- by_type.orchestrator.gated_git_commands contains 'git merge' (line 67); by_type.orchestrator.blocked_git_commands (lines 43-64) does NOT contain it.\n- Parent comparison (git show 17a1960^): the ONLY diff is the removed root 'git merge' line — all by_type and shared lists are byte-identical.\n\n### Step 3 — crosslink-guard.ts applyAgentTypeOverride: PASS\n- FAIL-CLOSED warnings present and loud ('!!! FAIL-CLOSED') for: (a) crosslinkDir null (lines 840-846), (b) CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE env unset (lines 847-856), (c) no by_type match (lines 862-869). All log via the existing guard log.\n- Gating semantics identical to parent: return config when no crosslinkDir; return config when no byType; apply blocked/gated/allowed lists + success log when byType exists. The old '!runtimeAgent' early return was functionally unreachable (resolveAgentType always returns a non-empty string, defaulting to 'builder'), and the new code reaches the identical outcome via the no-byType branch. No case returns a different config than before.\n- Exactly one hunk changed; loadConfig, defaults, resolveAgentType, and command-matching helpers untouched.\n- Syntax verified by inspection (balanced, valid optional-chaining computed member access, string concat). tsc/bun/node not runnable under the read-only sandbox, so compile-level verification was inspection-only.\n\n### Step 4 — load-path sanity: PASS\n- .crosslink/agent.json role is 'driver' here, so isAgentContext() is false at root and loadConfig applies the ROOT blocked list — which no longer contains merge. A fresh plugin load in this repo no longer hard-blocks 'git merge'.\n- CROSSLINK_AGENT_TYPE=orchestrator → by_type.orchestrator → merge gated on active issue. Env unset → FAIL-CLOSED logged, merge falls through to active-issue enforcement (strict). Reviewer/auditor remain hard-blocked in both TS-plugin (by_type) and agent-worktree (shared agent list) paths.\n\n### Confirmed explicitly\n(a) reviewer and auditor still hard-block merge (by_type lines 75/102 + shared agent list line 19); (b) the root list no longer blocks merge (lines 179-194); (c) gating logic in crosslink-guard.ts is unchanged apart from added logging (single hunk, behavior-equivalent).\n\n### SHOULD CONSIDER (non-blocking)\n- .opencode/plugins/crosslink-guard.ts:839-869 + .crosslink/hook-config.json (no by_type.builder entry) — a DRIVER-context session whose resolved type has no by_type entry (builder, or env unset → agent.type 'builder') now gets merge neither root-blocked nor per-role gated; it only passes active-issue enforcement. permissions.md:98 documents Builder merge = Blocked. In agent worktrees the shared agent list still hard-blocks builder, but a main-repo session launched as builder with an active issue can now merge. This is the agreed fall-through, but consider hardening with an explicit by_type.builder blocked list containing 'git merge' (or documenting that builder sessions must run in worktrees).\n- .claude/hooks/work-check.py:99-112 — the legacy Python hook consumes the same root config (driver context now consistently un-blocks merge) but has NO by_type handling: in agent contexts it applies the shared agent_overrides list (still contains merge) to ALL types, so an orchestrator under the Claude Code/Python path would still have merge hard-blocked. The fix only un-gates merge on the TS-plugin (opencode) path. Out of #173 scope; track separately if the Python path is still used.\n\n### NITS\n- crosslink-guard.ts:847-856 — the env-unset FAIL-CLOSED warning fires on every hook call even when resolution and by_type match correctly (noisy by design per the issue; consider once-per-session dedup).\n- Working-tree .crosslink/.last-hydrated-ref churn shows up in git status; not a defect.\n\n### NOTABLE POSITIVES\n- Strict scope discipline: exactly the two agreed files, one-line config removal, surgical plugin change.\n- Behavior-preserving refactor with the dead '!runtimeAgent' check removed without semantic change.\n- FAIL-CLOSED messages are loud, role-specific, and explain the operational consequence (e.g. 'orchestrator merge gating may be wrong').\n\nVerdict: CHANGES NOT REQUESTED. Fix meets agreed scope; two SHOULD-CONSIDER hardening notes.","created_at":"2026-08-04T03:51:21.402285922Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5Cw