{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":788,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:46:00.137692128Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"3b8274f4-d06e-415a-b1a8-aaab3bdf6237","comment_uuid":"6646dbc6-6244-4653-a097-c7123cd9e493","author":"OL2r","content":"RECURRING PATTERN (3rd occurrence, 2026-08-04 session #13): concurrent kickoff launches transiently clobber the main-repo local issues.db view. Symptom: after a kickoff launch, 'crosslink issue list' shows only 3-4 legacy issues; all hub issues (e.g. #154/#175-#178) resolve as 'not found'; launching additional kickoff agents against the clobbered DB fails with 'Issue #N not found'. The LAUNCH SUCCEEDS (worktree + hub intact); only the main-repo DB view collapses. Recovery: 'crosslink sync' re-hydrates (181 issues), all resolvable. Trigger confirmed: each kickoff launch sequence runs a hydration that rewrites the main DB (mtime == launch time). Mitigation used: launch agents SEQUENTIALLY with a sync between; do NOT race concurrent launches. Evidence: 06:23:25 clobber after r1 launch (r2/r3 failed); 06:35:52 clobber after r2 launch; 06:45 clobber after r3 launch. Related: #123/#124/#137, session-#11 episode.","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:46:00.131924084Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAB4JVvoL9M0EX/dNCr1n+6etQ2klBi3rMMqqR23xNzsGXay6yygPyV8jCS9q3zoK6IFQXQuXtHlXi0fvn6SM8BA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJ/GGhvLBNJeLww2MFuIGTXO7xaZfe5dUu+LwHbZ+ytksj0sT8oXfZoSnu0+lng4JxGscH/t86+PEwiKJ+qkwAU="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":789,"timestamp":"2026-08-04T06:55:48.700891721Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"c212e3bd-e79a-41b0-bd0b-679d4b8c3b83","comment_uuid":"88a4d730-b030-4a43-988d-46359c67b7af","author":"OL2r","content":"DESIGN REVIEW SYNTHESIS (session #13) — 3 independent reviewers, all CONDITIONAL. Design on #175 (builder pp3g-i81g) is DIRECTIONALLY SOUND but NOT implementation-ready as written.\n\nVERDICTS: r1 (hy3) CONDITIONAL — 3 blockers + 13 findings; r2 (luna) CONDITIONAL — 5 required fixes; r3 (big-pickle) CONDITIONAL PASS — 3 required fixes (R1-R3).\n\nCONVERGENCE (all 3 independently verified against live binary + v1.18.12 source):\n- Fork/pin strategy SOUND: sst/opencode=301->anomalyco/opencode reconciled; v1.18.12 pin correct; wrapper indirection + autoupdate:false is the right upgrade-survival shape.\n- Root-cause diagnosis EXACT: SessionRetry.policy unbounded Schedule.fromStepWithMetadata; ResponseStreamError->isRetryable:true; halt() surfaces ERROR only when schedule gives up.\n- Upgrade-wipe finding CONFIRMED by all 3: installed binary 1.18.12 (03:15 upgrade) wiped #145 patch; bug is LIVE NOW. autoupdate:false is absent from current config.\n- Retry-budget OFF-BY-ONE (r1 F9, r2 fix1, r3 R1): meta.attempt is 1-based RETRY count, so RETRY_MAX_ATTEMPTS=3 yields 4 POSTs, contradicting '<=3 POSTs' assertion. Must pin semantics: constant=total attempts with >=, or RETRY_MAX_RETRIES=2.\n- Non-atomic cp in §5.2 (r1 F10, r2 fix2, r3 N1): use same-filesystem mv per #145 proven pattern.\n\nCRITICAL DIVERGENCE — deadline SHAPE (must resolve before implementation):\n- r1 (hy3) BLOCKER B2: Option B total-completion deadline is the WRONG shape. Recommends Option A' = distinct longer per-chunk IDLE deadline for non-SSE branch (same mechanism as wrapSSE, own knob). Rationale: (a) idle timer also resets per chunk so hy3 F2 protection is identical; (b) detection latency far better (Option B with bodyTimeout=30min burns up to 90min across 3 attempts before ERROR; #145 interim detected in 300s); (c) Option B introduces NEW false-abort class: legit long STREAMING response with non-SSE content-type (Bedrock eventstream, ndjson, text/plain streaming) killed at 30min wall-clock. Total-completion is correct only for single-shot bodies; content-type cannot distinguish.\n- r3 (big-pickle) explicitly PASSES Option B (total-completion, 30min default < 1h overall timeout) as semantically correct.\n- r2 (luna) passes Option B directionally.\n\nOTHER BLOCKERS (r1): B1 — design patches only 1 of 2 shipped guard copies (provider.ts v1 path; packages/core/src/aisdk.ts v2 SessionRunner path has 2nd identical guard, no headerTimeout, raises plain Error not APIError). #145 byte patch neutralized BOTH; source patch must too, or prove v2 unreachable. B3 — blanket 3-attempt cap regresses deliberate rate-limit waiting (retry.ts honours retry-after; upstream tests wait >10min; FreeUsageLimitError/GoUsageLimitError say 'resets in 3 hours'). Scope budget by error class: tight cap for timeout/stream errors, preserve retry-after for 429/usage-limit. F5 — causal gap: live config timeout=1h (AbortSignal.timeout fires on stalled body per #145) yet #142 hung 10.9h with zero retries; stall may be ABOVE raw-body layer (llm.ts:373 fullStream, upstream #39968 parsed-stream stalls). Harness only tests raw-body layer — add turn-level wall-clock guard + instrument real path.\n\nREQUIRED BEFORE IMPLEMENTATION (priority order, r1):\n1. B3+F4 first, separately from fork: per-attempt retry logging (zero-risk, fixes operator-blindness root cause) + error-class-scoped budget. No blanket 3-attempt cap.\n2. F13 stopgap TODAY: set autoupdate:false + re-apply #145 byte patch (offsets shifted to 97992597/99193357) — box is vulnerable right now.\n3. B1: patch aiskd.ts too or prove v2 unreachable.\n4. B2: replace total-completion with idle-progress deadline (or document why not) — resolve divergence with r3.\n5. F5: reconcile 1h timeout vs 10.9h hang, or add turn-level guard.\n6. F6-F9: wrapBody pull() shape, sound timer/controller lifecycle, opt-in bodyTimeout, off-by-one fix.\n7. F10-F12: atomic install, build prereqs (workspace-root bun install, --skip-embed-web-ui decision, bun@1.3.14 pin), fork-identity marker + drift detection.\n8. Harness: stalled-but-not-dead test, gzip, real-provider capture, fork unit tests, grep-assert ERROR, R2/R3 test fixes.\n\nRECOMMENDATION: design revision round (implementer addresses blockers/findings, re-review), NOT implementation as written. Epic #156 chain paused at #154 gate pending operator decision.","created_at":"2026-08-04T06:55:48.692814616Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAhAU5fmuuDYWN0c92WsPveiPZ3hV+TUJ9YvJp0HNKDiK0w2vNGdJlJFJYQx9sX9XKTkecO6hEhHXQP9nh4uQyDw=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGMSVDVc35MimdY0JePgN1SjIkhC6YLf/xK75Za5G4qM/7Dxopqeb+sDXhKBGSjcqaleYO1rrL63/PVGPNC1oQU="}
