{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":831,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T23:22:34.871768306Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8d4d5b12-2ea3-452b-8708-5a5bf89714c0","comment_uuid":"8c37ee44-4c76-4bad-8edc-2e4334d6af28","author":"OL2r","content":"Completed: INDEPENDENT round-2 re-review of the revised #154 durable opencode silent-hang fix design (#180). Verdict CONDITIONAL, posted as --kind result to #182. Isolation preserved: did NOT read #176/#177/#178 or any other re-review sub-issue. Method: re-derived ~20 source citations from a real upstream v1.18.13 checkout (/tmp/opencode/opencode-upstream-r3) plus the live binary and config rather than trusting the change-log; all substance verified accurate, §0 byte-exact. CLOSED: F6, F9, F10, F12, F13, R1, R3, F8 (opt-in), F11 (substance), F5 (substantially). NOT CLOSED: 5 blocking conditions - V1 (B1: aisdk.ts hunk 4 references undeclared bodyIdleAbortCtl and leaves positional signals.find controller selection, so Patch B does not compile and mis-binds); V2 (R2: §7.1 sets bodyIdleTimeout=30000 behind timeout=15000 so the new deadline can never fire; test 6's 25s slow body is guaranteed to false-abort at 15s; test 9 unrunnable); V3 (F7: bodyAbsoluteTimeout callback has no stream controller so it can neither close nor error the stream, and never clears absoluteId on the idle path); V4 (B2: numeric chain compares chain-total to per-request timeout and fails the project's own 15-20m operator-timeout ladder); V5 (B3/F4: terminal WARN reports meta.attempt+1 = 4 POSTs contradicting the 3-POST invariant, and sits on a non-Effect Cause.done return). Plus 9 non-blocking findings (ZlibError unbounded, header passthrough undecided, no config-schema entry so bodyIdleTimeout typos are silently accepted, wrong F11 citation, F5 guard left optional, OPENCODE_CHANNEL/IS_PREVIEW interaction, drift-check spawn cost, TUI message mapping lost, matrix has no v2-patch row). NOTE: worktree crosslink db was not hydrated with hub issues (4 local rows only), so all crosslink issue commands were run against the main checkout at /home/claude-code/projects/ASES. REVIEW-ONLY: no project files modified.","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:22:34.865617332Z","kind":"handoff","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAsk3quNiYrFhEt363STSb6Wfb+q5iGX4i+VZ0tDZH5ttABLdU6+J6an4jzwEGAAmQG9y4yA1MHBlNH5kkDlERCA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFdR0MT6e+ABVCgQrFj4GhdpHGVSngjC0q4nVUuBHX3uUnjEbPQyblbpxDBm7S8nNoKjsTAAFdkyMPq0ClWLJAQ="}
{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":832,"timestamp":"2026-08-05T23:23:20.535756855Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"036319c2-0184-46ff-9ab1-7eeb54c44e65","comment_uuid":"c0913aef-b92d-4abf-aef8-09621239ce19","author":"OL2r","content":"OPERATOR ACTION REQUIRED — I accidentally ended the orchestrator's session. Cause: this worktree's .crosslink/issues.db was never hydrated with hub issues (only 4 local rows; 'crosslink issue show 182' returned 'not found' in the worktree, while 'crosslink sync' hydrated 187 issues into the MAIN checkout's db at /home/claude-code/projects/ASES/.crosslink/issues.db). To reach #182 at all I ran every crosslink issue command with workdir=/home/claude-code/projects/ASES. My final 'crosslink session end --notes ...' therefore resolved to the MAIN repo and ended Session #13 (the orchestrator's, working on #156, started 2026-08-04 05:46), releasing its lock on #156. My handoff notes were written onto that session. IMPACT: orchestrator session #13 is closed and the #156 lock is released; no issue data, comments, or files were lost or modified, and the #182 verdict is posted correctly and verified present. REMEDY for the orchestrator: 'crosslink session start && crosslink session work 156' to resume; the #156 lock can be re-acquired. My own worktree session (#1) is separate and is ended in the worktree. LESSON for the kickoff harness: worktrees created by kickoff do not inherit the hydrated issue db, so a sub-agent tasked to comment on a hub issue has no correct-by-construction way to do so from its own worktree — running crosslink from the parent checkout is the only route, and it silently targets the parent's session and lock state.","created_at":"2026-08-05T23:23:20.529434794Z","kind":"intervention","trigger_type":"manual_action","intervention_context":"re-review r1 of #180 on sub-issue #182; worktree crosslink db not hydrated; 'crosslink session end' executed with workdir=main checkout, ending orchestrator session #13 instead of wo