{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":983,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T06:17:04.255024756Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b22a89ff-e016-4eab-9282-4e69d8ca729f","comment_uuid":"9f312c1e-016f-4e3b-bc9f-f36719c672f6","author":"OL2r","content":"Result: retry-classification validation complete — classification alone ELIMINATES the compounding (4x -> 1x spawns), with two residual gaps. Committed ff25820, report at research/toolregistry-lazy-mcp/retry-classification/report.md.\n\nBEFORE/AFTER (matched runs, loaded host):\n- Test 1 control (original #213 proxy): 4 backend spawns / 2 persistent proxies / reconnect=YES / 12176-42518ms.\n- Test 2 classified (proxy_classified.py): 1 backend spawn / 1 persistent proxy / reconnect=NO / 4224-14471ms. Matched-run latency ratio 0.25-0.43 (classification removes 75% of spawns, 57-75% of latency).\n- Test 3 (proxy killed mid-call): reconnect STILL fires, recovers to success 5.0 — did not overcorrect at ToolRegistry layer.\n- Test 3B (backend killed mid-call): proxy's own respawn-retry STILL fires, recovers — did not overcorrect at proxy layer. Classifier keyed on RuntimeError('Invalid structured content...') does not swallow MCPError(-32000) connection failures (empirically verified, Probe 2).\n\nCENTRAL CLAIM: YES — classification eliminates the compounding. Residual single-failure cost = 1 spawn + forward + classify, ~1.35-2.2x the #213 success baseline (dominated by unavoidable single backend init).\n\nREMAINING GAPS (state the size):\n1. Error SHAPE degraded: ToolRegistry 0.15.0 builds ErrorResult only from a raised exception, and the raise is what fires connection.py:106 reconnect. So proxy-only classification cannot deliver BOTH no-reconnect AND ErrorResult — caller gets ToolCallResult whose result is a pydantic repr wrapping the full verbatim schema error (is_error=True present). Clean ErrorResult requires a ToolRegistry integration-layer change (out of scope).\n2. C2 variant unreachable: consistently-drifted backend (declaration+behaviour both diverged) is invisible to proxy-side classification — the RuntimeError fires inside ToolRegistry's client and connection.py:106 still fires (2 spawns/2 proxies). Classification alone cannot reach C2.\n\nCONCLUSION: classification alone suffices IF the requirement is bounded single-spawn cost. The heavier mitigation (periodic revalidation / fallback live-schema fetch) still has only the single-spawn residual (~0.8-1.6s normal load) + error-shape fix + C2 reach left to save. Pins: toolregistry 0.15.0, mcp 2.0.0, python 3.10. stdio-only scope.","created_at":"2026-08-06T06:17:04.224906008Z","kind":"result","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAF625UUlQgeLfIXsih57fZDJ9zA9PYHiZ5HQMUm19eyBCXxKuExfvMHnj7vG8EUjZZET1ZEpjibk0V2TBQNeRDQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQI5/illpNDlm9z6WQGTgfZUMlircxaYa12FrJrP5Xp4z6BhtQls8BUK5Shr8EJh8s2RUNPVk80grm7aS6z5bcQ8="}
