{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1008,"timestamp":"2026-08-06T07:22:44.855827634Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"7ef840e7-d516-4301-b94d-f02d6d30bb55","title":"INVESTIGATE (C2 gap): self-healing vs ToolRegistry client interception vs patch — decision-ready comparison of three candidate approaches to close the consistently-drifted-backend gap (Option A proxy self-heal, Option B interception point, Option C patch assessment)","description":"Investigation, NOT a build. Follow-on to #217 (retry-classification). C2 (consistently drifted backend) still costs 2 spawns/2 proxies because the triggering exception fires inside ToolRegistry's own client, past proxy visibility. Test three options: A) proxy-side self-healing (failure counter, N=1 immediate heal, capture live shape, update served manifest, verify no flapping on intermittent drift); B) ToolRegistry client interception point (full tracebacks, identify SDK vs ToolRegistry origin, check installed-source extension points, smallest PoC wrapper if viable, stop if no clean point); C) patch assessment (only if B fails — minimal connection.py change, diff size + upgrade fragility, PoC only). Deliverable: comparison report with A's before/after cost numbers + flapping check, B's yes/no + traceback + PoC size, C's diff/fragility if reached, one-paragraph recommendation. Proof-of-concept quality only; no upstream PR; stdio only. Evidence from output-schema-drift (merged) + retry-classification (merged).","priority":"medium","parent_uuid":"44a2f894-85dc-4396-a3c6-66dbc327ec3b","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBYq6TFrDoEpif8MYr5WdFnDmOHPjSTF49Oy7uzKmaP19DUoB9ZEy6nUDYKfYdk+2w0oYaThzmGsOnhGMPx0KQw="}
