{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1102,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T22:07:54.499329738Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"6101c872-7999-4b0b-99db-ad696270a619","title":"MODEL-AGREEMENT ADDITION to the quality index (follow-on to #190 registry; #181). OPERATOR-DIRECTED (2026-08-06): the natural experiment is already in play — adversarial-review workflows require multiple review models on the same brief, so agreement data is a zero-cost byproduct of the standing process. GOAL: (1) define a MODEL-AGREEMENT SCHEMA for the quality index — per-wave record: wave context (what was reviewed), claim classes (the findings), per-model verdict (found/not-found/disagreed), verdict-level AND finding-level agreement (finding-level is load-bearing — the B2 divergence was masked at verdict level: both CONDITIONAL but disagreed on the core issue), divergence notes; (2) FORMALIZE COLLECTION as part of the workflow — agreement table included in the standard review-wave closeout synthesis (the orchestrator already sees all verdicts at synthesis; recording agreement there is structuring existing work, not new work); collection must NOT gate the review flow; (3) STANDARDIZE — fixed claim-class taxonomy + verdict vocabulary so rows compare across waves; (4) BACK-FILL historical multi-model waves from the hub — #136/#137 (watcher reviews luna+big-pickle), #150-#153 (four-reviewer consensus on #145 patch), the three #154 design-review rounds (hy3/luna/big-pickle/mimo), #199 (hy3 on #196), pre-session model feedback (gemini-3.1-pro, north-mini-code); mark retroactive rows as lower-confidence (reconstruction, not standardized collection); (5) INTEGRATE into capability-mapping/Model-Routing-Matrix.md + registry. DELIVERABLE: draft schema + collection process + back-filled agreement table. PRESENT SCHEMA TO OPERATOR FOR APPROVAL before treating as canonical. Research-layer artifact (EDASES registry).","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9