{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1110,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T22:26:17.813364638Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"cd27746b-bdc6-4164-89c2-69271ada7ef9","title":"REVIEW r1 (hy3, edge-case/source lens) — WORKFLOW-TOPOLOGY PROPOSAL review. Review the proposal for adding review/evidence stops to the agent workflow. THE PROPOSAL (concise statement to review): (1) TWO PRINCIPLES: (a) reasoning certainty — claims crossing a role boundary must state WHY, WHAT they're based on, and HOW CERTAIN (guess/evidence-based/proven), including what was NOT tested; (b) cheapest-test-first — assumptions that gate decisions must be tested with the quickest cheapest discriminating test. (2) TOPOLOGY FINDING: in role-separated agent systems, decision-gating claims crossing an information-asymmetry boundary (producer can verify cheaply, thin consumer cannot) are the dominant unguarded failure point; the corrective is producer-side calibration + cheapest-test obligation. (3) WORKFLOW STOPS: STOP A (post-plan testability audit, L1 cheap), STOP B (pre-consumption result audit — the load-bearing gate at the producer-consumer edge), STOP C (targeted L2 re-verification, only for high-stakes decisions like install/merge). (4) MODEL-AGREEMENT COLLECTION: agreement data recorded as a zero-cost byproduct of the standing multi-model review workflow (#241). ASSESS: correctness, edge cases the proposal misses (what claims are NOT testable? where do the stops add cost? does STOP B introduce a new bottleneck? is the thin-orchestrator preserved?), feasibility in this stack, and the model-agreement collection design. RE-DERIVE where checkable. Verdict: PASS / CONDITIONAL / FAIL with specific findings. POST to THIS sub-issue. Do NOT read other reviewer sub-issues.","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAA