{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1140,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T22:38:03.447756115Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f734b060-f9f3-4fdb-a808-aa19bb13e99e","title":"READ-ONLY SURVEY: locate and summarize the ORIGINAL model-role documentation and prior work on agent roles (esp. the AUDITOR role, which has been built but figures little in recent workflow discussions). GOAL: understand the work that came before — the original role definitions, any historical role design docs, model-role assignments, and how the auditor was intended to fit. SCOPE (search this repo + related): (1) .opencode/agents/*.md (all four roles incl. auditor.md — summarize each role's current definition); (2) docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md + .opencode/permissions.md (role contract + permission matrix); (3) git history — look for the ORIGINAL role definitions (git log --all --oneline -- .opencode/agents/, find the first commits introducing roles, and any prior versions of the role docs); (4) any docs mentioning the auditor role's intended function (grep for 'auditor' across docs/, .crosslink/knowledge/, research/, capability-mapping/); (5) model-feedback docs + Model-Routing-Matrix.md — do they reference role assignments per model? (6) historical session/decision records about role design (e.g., #121 orchestrator role, #133/#134 subagent research, #136/#137 reviewer verdicts on the watcher — role-related). DELIVERABLE: a structured summary — (a) the four roles as originally defined (dates + first-commit refs), (b) the auditor role's documented purpose and how it differs from reviewer, (c) any model-to-role assignments in the historical docs, (d) notable prior decisions about role design. READ-ONLY: no file modifications. POST summary as --kind result to THIS sub-issue.","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAA