{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1146,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T22:40:22.422124615Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"b680ab23-cfe8-497f-949d-6b10e0d5205e","comment_uuid":"edd017a1-1d7a-4dea-b221-314327aba610","author":"OL2r","content":"Plan: Independent breadth/adversarial review of the workflow-topology proposal (the concise statement in #244). Approach: (1) ground in the actual workflow shapes by reading the three orchestration tiers (kickoff/swarm/sentinel), the adversarial-review pipeline, the orchestrator contract, the checkpoint/progress contract, reviewer-independence rule, and the thin-orchestrator rule; (2) read the #241 model-agreement schema §6 (collection process) to test the 'zero-cost byproduct' claim against its own steps; (3) assess each of the 6 axes — breadth coverage, workflow-shape fit (swarm/sentinel/long-running), L1/L2/L3 cost-model realism, STOP B bounce-back boundedness, model-agreement hidden costs, and adversarial counterexamples; (4) attempt to break the proposal with concrete counterexamples (self-audit paradox, cheapest-test trilemma, certainty-vocabulary regress, information-asymmetry inversion at the review edge). NO other reviewer sub-issues read (#242/#243/#245). Verdict: PASS/CONDITIONAL/FAIL with specific findings, posted --kind result to THIS sub-issue.","created_at":"2026-08-07T22:40:22.414065748Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABANmH0teEE/a8l0fTIlyRVx92+WsVetKxor5lLjxwXmkL3te1DNpLhU0KfF2lf1y+znOKupT6b4evOjSfNprjQBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL+2bPoYMtx2lwbEat/zhdWHBZTpHWFN+TOEinnTYkDjebEE