{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1150,"timestamp":"2026-08-07T22:41:54.035499530Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"8d4d5b12-2ea3-452b-8708-5a5bf89714c0","comment_uuid":"e09f184c-b2fb-47d8-9a77-dd0e459fe918","author":"OL2r","content":"Completed: independent breadth/adversarial review of workflow-topology proposal (#244). Verdict: CONDITIONAL. 7 findings (2 critical: STOP B has no defined performer / self-audit paradox; STOP B bounce-back unbounded) + 6 adversarial counterexamples (cheapest-test trilemma, certainty-vocabulary regress, STOP A penalizes legit-expensive plans, model-agreement prerequisite unmet, contamination is reverse-asymmetry, silent-hangs outside framing). Proposal directionally correct (topology finding is a genuine novel insight; both principles adoptable) but operationally incomplete — 8 hardening items required before the stops can be implemented. No other reviewer sub-issues read. Result posted --kind result to #244.","created_at":"2026-08-07T22:41:54.030033821Z","kind":"handoff","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABAI+dcEkgNX367ARCnahws5mYPk54EJ2SPPuAiFVI+lF8Lc+VlZk1NT/uptxLJTvuM1vhUeScmy6CzOsJkzIDjBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQEDicszFdYiPus7tHIY4wS8O86wrFFC/g9yDyzXt2PB861SuXI650imj/byeBC6TLS0VyaGVleWCNFPvv4YRjgs="}
