{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1312,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T04:57:07.455490066Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"4b7e8889-cb57-44de-ae8b-0ce0c26b0a26","title":"DOC: record the chained/pipe-command allowlist gotcha in the playbook + ORCHESTRATOR.md — the bash allowlist matches the command PREFIX, so any pipe chain is denied even when every segment is individually allowed","description":"EVIDENCE (2026-08-08, Phase-2 auditor laguna pp3g-7uA3 on #264): the call 'rtk git show af350f49:.../intercept_poc.py | grep -v ... | grep -v ... | wc -l' was DENIED with 'The user has specified a rule which prevents you from using this specific tool call' even though the allowlist permits 'rtk *', 'git *', 'grep *'-style prefixes. ROOT CAUSE: the OpenCode bash allowlist matches the command STRING PREFIX; a pipe ('|') breaks the prefix match, so the chain fails as a whole even when each component command is individually allowed. Same class of failure as the orchestrator's earlier 'chained read' denials. FIX: document in .crosslink/knowledge/agent-orchestration-playbook.md (the §5.7 permission/bounded-signals section that already notes prefix-granularity allowlisting) and docs/ORCHESTRATOR.md (permission-matrix notes): (a) chained/piped commands are denied at the matcher; (b) agents should use a single tool invocation per command, or the Read tool for files, or rtk/git with flags rather than pipes; (c) this is by-design (prefix-scoped allowlist), not a bug. Doc-only task, low priority.","priority":"low","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNWSB888xPD2938kBnWivxe87rYryEJUbOq7JXAms7vfxDZs7jn36sjiCrutxSRyT3b+Ym5wIYqKE3IW1s7UFQc="}
