{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1333,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T05:39:46.638735125Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"f8b231ce-ae2a-440c-9b41-f5ef624a6ac7","title":"PROCESS FIX: enforce the 'commit volatile build artifacts before cleanup' obligation. ROOT CAUSE (2026-08-08 incident): the #154 durable-fork verified binary (sha 6e0e282b) + safeIterable-patched source tree lived ONLY in /tmp/opencode/fork-build. Issue #209 step 1 explicitly required 'EXPORT/COMMIT first — copy the patched fork source + unit tests + harness + patch files into THIS worktree (or commit the /tmp/fork-build as a branch), so nothing depends on volatile /tmp' — this was ONLY PARTIALLY executed: fork/ (patch + harness + tests) was committed, but the APPLIED SOURCE TREE, the safeIterable commit (98dfe4a), and the BUILT BINARY never were. A disk cleanup wiped /tmp/opencode (11G), destroying the only copies of the verified artifact + root-cause fix. The fix was recovered only because the opencode session DB (opencode.db) embedded the tool calls that applied it. FIXES: (1) codify a hard rule: any build artifact (compiled binary, patched source tree, generated output) that is decision-gating MUST be committed to a git branch before the session/agent that created it ends — never leave artifacts only in /tmp; (2) audit current in-flight workstreams for /tmp-only decision-gating artifacts and export them (e.g. #154 rebuild #270 must commit the rebuilt fork source + binary); (3) add a closeout checklist item in SESSION-END.md / handoff template: 'verified all decision-gating artifacts are in git, not /tmp'; (4) consider a cheap staleness/cleanup guard so 'crosslink kickoff cleanup' or disk-clearing never silently destroys uncommitted build state (link #227). Related: #154, #209, #270, #227, #125.","priority":"high","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAA