{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1357,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T05:55:55.110102367Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"07cb8b62-2ba1-446c-977b-940024864c56","comment_uuid":"dc52cae0-85ce-422a-87db-7a97dbbe2ede","author":"OL2r","content":"PLAN: Close all Phase-2 audit gaps on the C2 investigation (#228). Consolidates the two independent CONDITIONAL PASS verdicts (hy3 #263, big-pickle #265). Each item lists: the gap, the closing action, the verification, and which audit flagged it.\n\n== G1 [HIGH] PoC-size arithmetic non-reconcilable (hy3 R2/C3, big-pickle R1) ==\nGap: §5.3 headline '48 code lines' unexplained (components 5+20+22+10 = 57); table '99' mislabeled (strict code 64); §10.4 '~23-line' inconsistent; propagated to #228 result comment + dispatch briefs.\nClose: (1) add committed counter script tests/measure_poc_size.py (tokenize-based, stated rule: non-blank/non-comment/non-docstring, post-shebang) writing counts to a log; (2) rewrite §5.3 table with the script's output: total 147, strict code 64, mechanism-proper 57 (excl 6 imports + 1 constant), per-component counts; (3) fix §8/§11/§10.4 citations; (4) post corrected figures on #228 result comment and note the correction.\nVerify: run measure_poc_size.py; assert components sum to mechanism total; assert table == script output.\n\n== G2 [HIGH] Option B pre-absorbed claim is inferred, not tested (hy3 C1, big-pickle R3) ==\nGap: §8 'works in every tested session state (fresh or pre-absorbed)' — only fresh B2 was run.\nClose: run a B2b pre-absorbed phase (copy the A2b pattern: absorb the stale schema first, then invoke). Record spawn/proxy/reconnect/latency + whether interception still fires pre-absorbed. \nVerify: B2b passes at 1 spawn/1 proxy/no reconnect with verbatim ErrorResult; if it does not, correct §8 to state pre-absorbed is inferred-but-untested.\nAlternative (accepted if B2b impossible): relabel §8 as 'argued from mechanism'.\n\n== G3 [HIGH] Recommended option's upgrade fragility unassessed (hy3 C2, big-pickle systemic) ==\nGap: Option B overrides a private method (_call_persistent) and duplicates its body (intercept_poc.py:86-103 vs connection.py:101-111, incl. dropped logger.warning); the brief scoped fragility to Option C only, so the WINNING option shipped un-assessed.\nClose: (1) add §5.5 upgrade-fragility paragraph citing the concrete coupling (private method, duplicated body, dropped logger.warning, no backoff/lock/telemetry divergence detection); (2) qualify §11's 'dependency-free and patch-free' — state it is dependency-free but NOT patch-free: it couples to a private version-bound internal of toolregistry 0.15.0/mcp 2.0.0; (3) add a re-validation trigger note for toolregistry/mcp upgrades (ties to G8).\nVerify: the paragraph's line citations reproduce (intercept_poc.py:86-103, connection.py:101-111).\n\n== G4 [MEDIUM] n=1 latencies with no n stated (hy3 C4, big-pickle R3) ==\nGap: §7 latencies are single-shot with no n and no variance, while citing #213's n=2/n=3 ranges.\nClose: re-run the key latency phases (A2 fresh, B2 PoC, A1 control) to n>=3 under normal load where feasible; state n per row; if variance is high, report range not point.\nVerify: §7 table states n for every latency row; cross-document baseline rows carry their source n.\n\n== G5 [MEDIUM] Flapping check rests on a single heal event; N never varied (hy3 C6) ==\nGap: only N=1 tested; A3 had 1 heal event total; the builder's own plan committed to 'vary N to find the flapping threshold' but dropped it.\nClose: run A3 with N=2 and N=3 (two extra phase variants) to confirm no heal-back/thrashing at higher thresholds; record the threshold sweep result. \nVerify: for each N, no flapping observed and the result row records the N used.\n\n== G6 [MEDIUM] Asymmetric test depth — B under-tested vs A (hy3 C5) ==\nGap: A got 3 phases/11 calls; B got 1 traceback + 1-call PoC; no warm-call or other-tool-untouched for B.\nClose: add B2 warm-call measurement (repeated invocation on the intercepted session) and an other-tool-untouched check for B (a second tool unaffected after the B2 failure), mirroring A2.\nVerify: warm-call latency recorded; other-tool success recorded.\n\n== G7 [MEDIUM] Two reusable constraints trapped in the phase report (hy3 S5, big-pickle R2) ==\nGap: (a) C2 exception is SDK-origin at mcp/client/session.py:1110 and ToolRegistry 0.15.0 has NO failure-class distinction (connection.py:106 catches bare Exception); (b) register_from_mcp hardcodes MCPConnectionManager at integration.py:323, so any connection-layer customisation requires manual registration assembly.\nClose: promote both into the umbrella document (docs/research/Identifier-First Tool Calling.md, under epic #212) and/or a versioned crosslink knowledge page.\nVerify: umbrella/knowledge page contains both facts with version tags.\n\n== G8 [MEDIUM] Version-bound findings carry no expiry marker (hy3 S6, big-pickle systemic) ==\nGap: Option B conclusions valid only for toolregistry==0.15.0 + mcp==2.0.0, depend on private internals; §8/§11 state them unconditionally.\nClose: (1) add version-validity lines to §8/§11 ('valid for toolregistry 0.15.0 / mcp 2.0.0; verify on upgrade'); (2) file a re-validation trigger issue under epic #212 for toolregistry/mcp upgrades.\nVerify: version-validity lines present; re-validation issue exists with correct parent.\n\n== G9 [LOW] Process hygiene (hy3 R8, big-pickle R4) ==\nGap: 'Plan: <placeholder test>' comment on #228 never annotated; #228 result comment conflated '147/48'; §5.2 citation _call_per_request (113-121) wrong (113-118); kickoff template writes DONE for read-only roles.\nClose: (1) annotate/retract the placeholder comment; (2) correct the #228 result comment; (3) fix the §5.2 citation; (4) kickoff-template fix (remove write-DONE step for read-only roles) — track separately as its own issue.\nVerify: placeholder annotated; result comment corrected; citation matches source.\n\n== G10 [LOW] No explicit Limitations section (hy3 R5) ==\nGap: absences invisible (no B pre-absorbed before this plan, no B warm, N=1 only, single host, stdio only).\nClose: add a §Limitations block listing exactly what was NOT tested, converting silent gaps to declared scope.\nVerify: Limitations block present and enumerates the items in this plan's G2/G4/G5/G6 pre-close state.\n\n== CLAIM-VERIFICATION PASS (covers 'verify all the claims') ==\nAfter G1-G10: run the full re-derivation one more time across the revised report: all timing/spawn rows, all source-line citations (session.py:1110, 1064; client.py:133; connection.py:97-111, 106; integration.py:223, 323; session.py:1086, 1247, 1276), md5 corpus identity, traceback-origin, verbatim ErrorResult. Each claim must cite the committed artifact; no claim without an artifact. This pass is the 'verified' gate before the report is merged.\n\n== OWNERSHIP ==\nOne builder dispatch on #277 executes G1-G10 + the claim-verification pass in a single worktree on the existing feature branch. Model: deepseek-v4-flash. Timeout: 45m. After execution, the revised report is merged to main and #228/#263/#265/#277 are updated.\n\n== REVIEW GATE (this plan) ==\nBefore execution, big-pickle reviews THIS plan against the audit criteria: does it address every gap in the hy3 #263 and big-pickle #265 verdicts, every discrepancy (PoC size, tested-vs-inferred), and the claim-verification requirement? Reviewer: big-pickle, read-only, on this issue. Any plan gap found is to be filed back before execution begins.","created_at":"2026-08-08T05:55:55.104383438Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABALEcN9vYZUdc5NvJKPWAvg2VR+bEQvFjeQmR4h44BKHCq5/Ih8JO+IP0dPREYBWw0oQAiLdeIQVQr3HKuqonrBg=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQKWBlFF5oO96+haD41dhpdjTnCxSyA62oUQCyH9+FeOlO0AhVC5nHFkMJdNJ0PkVY56nhbCoKLces+0qKXdX/Ak="}
