{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1367,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T06:27:21.623769626Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"d0e0f7ba-1352-43ca-95c1-17d68d618fa2","title":"DOC: reconcile playbook §5.4/§6.1 orchestrator-direct-watch with §5.8 auditor-mediated monitoring + document systemd watcher layer","description":"EVIDENCE (2026-08-08, reliability-epic agent conversation, relayed by operator): an agent working the reliability epic corrected its mental model to 'auditor = liveness canary + divergence verifier; orchestrator polls the auditor for updates, does not peer into the builder's pane as routine'. It then flagged a doc/intent drift: playbook §5.4 (Missed check-in escalation: 'investigate: ps -o pid,etime,time,stat -p <pid>, check session status') and §6.1 ('a missing checkpoint past the expected interval is a stalled-agent signal — investigate before the timeout') read as orchestrator-side direct checkpoint/staleness watching, contradicting §5.8 ('staleness causes the pre-positioned AUDITOR to act; it flags to the orchestrator; the orchestrator owns the bounded action set'). ROOT CAUSE: §5.4/§6.1 predate the workflow-topology formalization and were never reconciled after §5.8 landed. FIX SCOPE (operator-directed): (a) reconcile §5.4/§6.1 with §5.8 auditor-mediated monitoring — the orchestrator's routine monitoring is auditor-mediated; orchestrator-side ps/investigate is the fallback when no auditor is present or on auditor flag; (b) document the FULL three-layer monitoring model so the orchestrator has complete information both for itself and to pass to subagents: systemd watcher (ases-kickoff-notify.timer/service, §6.4) = mechanical process liveness; pre-positioned AUDITOR = claim-vs-evidence divergence verification; orchestrator = bounded action set (investigate/nudge/stop-resume) + single integration point. NUANCE: auditor flags to the ORCHESTRATOR (never the operator directly); the orchestrator surfaces only decisions to the operator. Doc-only task; fix lands within reliability epic #156 playbook reconciliation, separate from the #266 pipe-chain gotcha (already committed c055db78).","priority":"low","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHK9UaTZvD8BNePoseI4CMaPYQj7iWNl0jIiJY1dKNgsO1bnnq0r0gwnudaDHVrzzp6nYEsvwag9r5fw7KBBcgA="}
