{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1392,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T07:19:06.708401564Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"ac8ea82a-64d6-4339-895d-b13bd7cbf522","title":"DOC amendment (operator decision, 2026-08-08): time-based commit cadence for UNAVOIDABLY LONG TASKS ONLY. CONTEXT: work-loss synthesis — atomic-split (commit-sized tasks, commit-at-landing) solves the general case; the residual gap is the irreducible long phase (a 40-min build, a 30-min matrix, a long verification run) that cannot be atomized further, where an agent death loses all work since the last milestone commit. OPERATOR DECISION: add a NARROW time-based commit rule that applies ONLY to unavoidably long phases — NOT a general cadence rule (atomicity covers everything else). RULE (to codify in agent-orchestration-playbook.md, adjacent to §5.9): for a single phase estimated >~30-45 min that cannot be split, the agent MUST commit progress at time intervals (~every 15 min): evidence logs, intermediate outputs, WIP notes, partial results — anything durable that would otherwise be lost on death. Purpose: (a) work preservation — a death loses at most one interval of work, not the whole phase; (b) liveness evidence — commits are ground-truth artifacts the pre-positioned AUDITOR can join against (stronger than checkpoint comments alone). DO NOT apply to normal commit-sized tasks (atomic-split already guarantees commit points). Keep it brief — a short subsection under §5.9 or a §5.9 extension; docs-only. Ref #271 (parent rule), #156.","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFc6LX+N2nBM0Uz1xRbCEarWA4XMm/POeecMJybPgvOFJTutnavVjkmTNu0415BfjKvbsIMI4CXec7DHqCFmdwo="}
