{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1450,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T17:27:59.239536153Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"dbee82c3-daf5-46f4-a91b-ce115ed278d9","comment_uuid":"6d1a895f-ff07-4e00-8361-a43a1d7d5773","author":"OL2r","content":"ATOMIC-MATRIX DIRECTION (orchestrator, operator-requested): make the matrix resumable at row granularity so an agent death loses at most one row, not the whole run. ADOPT THIS IN THE RUNNING TASK (or a continuation): (1) the matrix is 16 independent rows (each spawns own server+client); (2) after EACH row completes, append 'rowN: PASS/FAIL <brief evidence>' to a results ledger (e.g. fork/results/matrix-ledger.log) and git-commit it (per #286 §5.9.1 per-phase commits — here applied per-row); (3) if the process dies at row 8, the ledger has rows 1-7 committed; a continuation agent reads the ledger, skips completed rows, resumes from the first incomplete row; (4) per-row artifacts already exist (client-rowN.out, server-rowN.log) — the ledger just records which rows PASSED and where to resume. This is a script-level change to the run loop (commit after each row), not a redesign. NOTE: the commit c7d6e24 is source-only (all 6395 files under fork/opencode-src/ — the binary, harness, tests, INSTALL-PREP were NOT committed because the task-1 agent died before copying them; they survive in /tmp/opencode/ + the fork-build repo). The #271 commit-all is only PARTIALLY satisfied — after the matrix, task 3 must re-commit the binary + harness + results. If you are mid-run without the ledger, add it now for the remaining rows.","created_at":"2026-08-08T17:27:59.230760016Z","kind":"observation","signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABArXiI/qk9HEAgsNiicJ/lodsHSlN9sKvwadivW7D17KkMvsnC3+7avhPVIDFoGmlhsNABhX366GyFeqHDR/KTBQ=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:t