{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1456,"timestamp":"2026-08-08T18:02:26.310813685Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"2a795a46-f144-4ebd-9cc4-1b22fd436eed","title":"VALIDATE (catalog scale vs connector residency): does a runtime know N tools while keeping physical connector-process residency proportional to K (used), not N (configured/refreshed) — 6 tests + addendum (stdio only, reuse lazy proxy + pinned venv)","description":"Phase-5 completion for the identifier-first line. Validates the session-boundary confirmation model's cost assumption: catalog knowledge N decoupled from physical connector residency O(K), K<=N. 6 tests: (1) catalog acquisition stays backend-lazy (scope guard, stop-and-investigate if violated); (2) refresh residency single-N with teardown off/on (proxy vs backend reported SEPARATELY, never collapsed); (3) N-sweep 1/5/10/20/50 x sequential/concurrent x teardown off/on, resident-after is the decisive measure; (4) sparse-use N=20 K=3, headline row = 17 refreshed-but-never-called tools' proxies, plus connector identity/reuse tracking across acquire->call1->call2; (5) catalog invalidation via notifications/tools/list_changed (long-standing MCP capability since 2024-11-05, already declared false in the Round-1 initialize artifact; characterizes current behavior, does NOT design a fix) + no-signal stale-catalog baseline; (6) immediate teardown as diagnostic boundary (NOT the full idle-timeout feature). Addendum A-E applied: Test 5 split into invalidation-test + stale-baseline; record sync/async calling mode + daemon-thread count per connector + persistence config state (verify actual parameter name in installed toolregistry==0.15.0 source) + pinned versions per run; strong-pass criterion reframed as 'resident resources bounded by workload/policy, not proportional to N' (not literal count==K); connector identity tracking. Residency rules: resident = still running holding resources; briefly-defunct within 2s grace OK; beyond grace = lifecycle finding. Out of scope: full configurable idle-timeout feature, invalidation-strategy design, unreachable-connector failure design, non-stdio, re-testing output-schema drift. Deliverable: report with Test 1-6 results, required data tables, one-sentence scaling conclusion (scales with N or K?), architectural conclusion per Strong/Conditional/Fail criteria.","priority":"high","parent_uuid":"44a2f894-85dc-4396-a3c6-66dbc327ec3b","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGi8TuUqe/mZkz6fKvwv1y1P/xe9K6q2cKbEyJyO/JacZQA5odgIN2pY+f73BPNgmVxMpux2DWmLpR20dQcf1Qg="}
