{"agent_id":"OL2r","agent_seq":1556,"timestamp":"2026-08-09T15:46:57.221396993Z","event":{"type":"IssueCreated","uuid":"497dbef5-069b-4086-b9f5-f2c54953d182","title":"DOC: agent tooling & permission enforcement — current state write-up for external review","description":"DESCRIPTION: Write a self-contained markdown document describing the current agent tooling / permission-enforcement system in ASES, for external review (to be sent to models inside and outside this environment). Scope: (1) what software we use (opencode + the pp3g fork, the crosslink fork CLI, the claude wrapper, rtk, sqlite3, the three in-repo guard plugins, user-level model-whitelist plugin); (2) what we are trying to do (four-role permission model — orchestrator/builder/reviewer/auditor — with a deliberately read-only reviewer+auditor, workflow-topology pre-positioned auditor, git write discipline gated on active issues); (3) why this specific set of tools/plugins (each layer's job and the failure it prevents: #33677 edit:deny gap, git push/rebase discipline, active-issue gating, token-saving rtk rewrite, model whitelist); (4) the identified problem areas: THREE-SURFACE kickoff enforcement (hook-config allowed_bash_prefixes vs kickoff.allowed_tools vs agent .md permission block), per-type asymmetry (build_allowed_tools is identical for all agent types — auditor-only grants not expressible), two-surface inconsistency (agent .md says 'opencode *' but kickoff template grants less), #33677 gap requiring orchestrator-guard. Canonical sources to verify against: .opencode/opencode.json, .opencode/agents/*.md, .opencode/plugins/*.ts, .crosslink/hook-config.json, /home/claude-code/projects/crosslink/crosslink/src/commands/kickoff/{prompt.rs,helpers.rs,launch.rs}, ~/.config/opencode/plugins/plugin.ts. Deliverable: docs/research/agent-tooling-and-permission-enforcement.md (proposed path; builder may adjust per repo conventions). READ-ONLY investigation of sources; write only the deliverable doc. Ref: workflow-topology design record docs/research/Workflow Topology Design and Reasoning Record.md, #156 epic, #298 (sleep grant precedent), #313 findings.","priority":"medium","created_by":"OL2r"},"signed_by":"SHA256:txtxRbCGncxPs5YVqhd0abUgfcruU3ze6o9USZ9e9ck","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgBrkJWbwQmXES5+ltWRxRKeJmS2PIO3BfyCG5CwZdt0oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBnfI8gRgbUOaI/WWtqhfNCCrDa6vCdK4td6JwuJSi63jxgxfbl+O/V/xnwEEAG34tTppceFH/5/UnpN8KT8wwo="}
